1
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:07,090
[mic feedback]

2
00:00:07,883 --> 00:00:11,845
[host] Congratulations to everyone
who survived the first Main Match.

3
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:15,807
We will now begin the first Seeker Vote.

4
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:19,061
-Seeker?
-[Jieun] What?

5
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,104
-Seeker Vote?
-[Jieun] What?

6
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,316
[Horseking] It turns out
there's a Seeker. [gasps]

7
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:25,526
[Eunsil] What's going on?

8
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,403
[host] The Seeker is a hidden architect

9
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:31,406
who creates chaos and controls
the course of the chase,

10
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:34,826
secretly working
to prevent the players from winning.

11
00:00:35,536 --> 00:00:36,578
[scoffs]

12
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,915
Someone has been fooling us.

13
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,961
[host] Before the Seeker Vote,
we have an announcement.

14
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:48,048
In yesterday's Main Match,
"Cops and Robbers,"

15
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,758
the Seeker's mission...

16
00:00:52,678 --> 00:00:53,762
SEEKER'S MISSION
SUCCESS

17
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:55,055
...was completed successfully.

18
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:57,057
[chuckles nervously]

19
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,643
[ZZONE] It was so shocking.
I had no idea at all.

20
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:02,312
-[host] By completing their mission...
-I just got chills.

21
00:01:02,396 --> 00:01:05,566
...the Seeker will gain a special benefit.

22
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,317
[Jimin] I was completely caught off guard.

23
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:12,406
[Ddolddol] I realized the Seeker
was already steering the game in a way

24
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:15,033
to give themselves the upper hand.

25
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:19,079
THE SEEKER WAS AMONG THEM YESTERDAY

26
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:22,791
[Jieun] I realized
you can't trust anyone now.

27
00:01:22,874 --> 00:01:25,669
Are they trying to sabotage
their own team?

28
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,171
-I think so.
-"Prevent the players from winning."

29
00:01:30,382 --> 00:01:32,551
[sighs] I hate games
where you have to think.

30
00:01:33,135 --> 00:01:35,262
-It's you, isn't it?
-No, no, no.

31
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:38,599
[host] Excluding Gyeong Sujin,
the Seeker is someone

32
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:40,142
among the 12 players.

33
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,561
Then, the Seeker could be
among the eliminated players too.

34
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:45,188
They could be here or over there.

35
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:46,648
THE SEEKER COULD BE IN PRISON

36
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:49,526
Starting now, prison visits are allowed,

37
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:51,111
and players in prison

38
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,155
can vote as well.

39
00:01:56,116 --> 00:01:58,201
If the Seeker is successfully caught,

40
00:01:58,285 --> 00:02:01,038
the Seeker will immediately become
an elimination candidate.

41
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,666
However, if you fail to catch the Seeker,

42
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:08,337
the player with the most Seeker Votes
and the player chosen by the Seeker

43
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:12,591
will go to the Death Match
through an Elimination Vote.

44
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:16,803
The Seeker Vote will start
in an hour from now.

45
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,390
-[Ddolddol] Starting now?
-[Jieun] Now?

46
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:21,933
[Joonsu] Right away?

47
00:02:22,017 --> 00:02:25,145
[ZZONE] So this is why
it's called Deadly Tag.

48
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:26,229
SEEKER VOTE

49
00:02:27,314 --> 00:02:28,315
This is intense.

50
00:02:29,483 --> 00:02:32,819
[Ddolddol] If the Seeker picks me,
I'm at a disadvantage.

51
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:35,238
And if I get falsely accused
of being the Seeker,

52
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:36,573
I'm still in a bad spot.

53
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:38,659
[Junseo] I don't know who it is,

54
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,452
but I feel like I'm being toyed with.

55
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:45,791
I'm worried that this will affect
people with preconceptions,

56
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:50,253
and they'll automatically think,
"A spy? Park Jimin must be the one."

57
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:52,506
It was giving me such a headache.

58
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:55,801
[Pani Bottle] I think their quest
was definitely designed

59
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:58,220
-to make their team lose.
-Right.

60
00:02:58,303 --> 00:02:59,805
Otherwise, nothing would benefit them.

61
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,473
PLAYERS IN PRISON GUESS SEEKER'S MISSION

62
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:02,683
-Make their team lose...
-Yeah.

63
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:04,559
-...and not to go to prison.
-And they survive.

64
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,353
Maybe that's their mission.

65
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:08,730
Then, if we narrow it down,
it's not the cops.

66
00:03:08,814 --> 00:03:10,649
-It's not the cops.
-Yeah, it's not a cop.

67
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,275
I don't think it's Jimin or Jieun.

68
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:13,360
It's not us either.

69
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:14,986
-Right, because we're here.
-Yeah.

70
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,071
It's not us either.

71
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,115
If the Seeker fails,

72
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:21,702
does this mean their mission
gets revealed before the vote?

73
00:03:21,785 --> 00:03:25,163
Then, they must've not revealed it
because they were successful yesterday.

74
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:27,332
[ZZONE] Yeah, I think you're right.

75
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:31,086
If they failed,
the mission would've been revealed today,

76
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,879
but they succeeded yesterday.

77
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,172
If we vote now,

78
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:35,966
-it would just be on hunches.
-[Jaegyun] Exactly.

79
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,384
-Pretty much.
-Yeah.

80
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:39,136
No way.

81
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,679
[Eunsil] I don't think we can choose now.

82
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:45,517
We had no idea
what the Seeker's mission was.

83
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,436
We had no proof or hunches.

84
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:49,604
And no one really seemed suspicious.

85
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,691
[Jaegyun] Honestly, I have no idea.

86
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:56,153
So from that point on,
I talked with people more.

87
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:57,946
PLAYERS VISIT THE PRISON

88
00:03:58,029 --> 00:03:59,573
-Did you hear about the Seeker?
-We did.

89
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:03,493
We discussed and concluded
that the Seeker's role was clearly

90
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:06,830
to make their team lose
and avoid getting voted out.

91
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,457
-That was our guess.
-Their mission.

92
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,916
So, the Seeker lost?

93
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,711
It doesn't matter to them
if their team wins or loses.

94
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:14,546
That's irrelevant to them.

95
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:17,340
[Pani Bottle] We were thinking the Seeker

96
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,592
-wasn't a cop.
-It's not a cop.

97
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:21,178
[Pani Bottle] Why?
Because all the cops won.

98
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:23,138
The people in prison are guessing

99
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:25,223
the Seeker is not among the cops

100
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:27,976
because the cops
all worked together and won.

101
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:31,062
I don't really understand
why Pani Bottle and Yang Dail

102
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,482
-came to that conclusion.
-Right.

103
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:35,817
[Ddolddol] If they were a cop,
they would've done their mission

104
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,736
-without the others knowing.
-That's possible.

105
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:39,488
[Ddolddol] It may not be about
winning or losing.

106
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:42,991
Maybe the mission was
to put together your team as you want

107
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,242
and win the game.

108
00:04:44,326 --> 00:04:46,244
-That could be true.
-[Jimin] If that's the case...

109
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:49,122
-So, we can't rule out the cops.
-[Jieun] You're right.

110
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:51,708
What makes me think
the Seeker could be a cop is,

111
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:55,712
Eunsil was the Narcotics cop,
and the three of us were Drug Criminals.

112
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:59,299
It would be easier for a female cop
to handle the other women.

113
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:00,842
[ZZONE] That does seem pretty fishy.

114
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:05,013
Maybe they chose people
who would be easier to control.

115
00:05:05,764 --> 00:05:07,182
This keeps bothering me.

116
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:10,936
"A hidden architect who creates chaos"
and "prevents the players from winning."

117
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:14,064
Exactly. Look, as an architect,
they can plan things out.

118
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:17,234
Then, they might have formed
the cops team.

119
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,568
Exactly.

120
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:20,028
[Jaegyun] I can't stop thinking

121
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:21,738
about the word "architect."

122
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,448
Whatever the mission was,

123
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:27,911
there's no way such strong players
would've all been selected as cops.

124
00:05:29,246 --> 00:05:31,373
[dealer] Please point to one card
of your choice.

125
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:33,250
DRUG CRIMINAL, ASSAULT CRIMINAL, BURGLAR

126
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:35,126
CI, VIOLENT CRIMES, NARCOTICS

127
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:37,170
Please point to one card of your choice.

128
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:40,006
-This one.
-Is this the card?

129
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,758
CRIMINALS NEVER HAD ANY COP CARDS TO PICK

130
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:44,219
Please point to one card of your choice.

131
00:05:45,554 --> 00:05:50,851
COPS COULD NEVER BECOME CRIMINALS

132
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:53,228
[host] The Seeker's Mission
will now be revealed.

133
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:58,692
According to the rules of Deadly Tag,
you have been selected as the Seeker.

134
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:06,074
[dealer] Please choose
one key number from 1 to 14.

135
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:08,618
PLAYERS EACH CHOSE A DIFFERENT KEY
UPON RECEIVING FUNDS

136
00:06:09,661 --> 00:06:11,788
[♪ mysterious music playing]

137
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:18,920
[host] In the Main Match,
"Cops and Robbers,"

138
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:23,133
your mission is
to make the three cops win.

139
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:26,636
Select three players
who will play the role of cops.

140
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:30,015
MAKE THE THREE COPS WIN
SELECT THREE PLAYERS TO BE COPS

141
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,933
[dealer] Put the three player cards
in the envelope.

142
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:33,643
CLOSE TO THE SEEKER'S MISSION OBJECTIVE

143
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:36,730
The odds were pretty high
that I'd become a cop,

144
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:38,815
because there were seven cards left.

145
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,942
I just wish I knew who was before me.

146
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,068
-[ZZONE] The order?
-[Horseking] Yes.

147
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,613
You were likely after me.
Kim Ddolddol. Then, Horseking,

148
00:06:44,696 --> 00:06:46,740
So you picked that when you went in?

149
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,242
I was the first one to go in,
and I got Good Citizen.

150
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:51,745
And then, I picked Good Citizen
right after that.

151
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,371
You're right. Two Good Citizens in a row.

152
00:06:53,455 --> 00:06:54,789
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol.

153
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,916
Mr. Horseking.

154
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,251
You are a Good Citizen.

155
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:00,420
TWO GOOD CITIZENS IN A ROW
AT THE START BY CHANCE

156
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:02,339
[Horseking] According to the odds,
it doesn't make sense.

157
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:05,634
The dealer told me to only choose
and said he'd flip the card.

158
00:07:05,717 --> 00:07:09,638
That's when I started thinking
that they could all be the same cards.

159
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:12,974
If you look at it that way,
ruling out the cops doesn't make sense.

160
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:14,392
[ZZONE] You have a point.

161
00:07:14,476 --> 00:07:16,019
That cop team was

162
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:17,979
-just too strong.
-[ZZONE] It was ridiculous.

163
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:20,315
[Horseking] It was as if pieces
of a puzzle were falling into place.

164
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:21,399
THE SEEKER IS A COP?

165
00:07:21,483 --> 00:07:23,860
If the architect is one of the cops,

166
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:26,696
they've done their job
because the cops won.

167
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:33,620
I'm just going to say what I think.

168
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:36,623
If I dare to speak my mind,

169
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:39,167
I have a feeling it's Sanghyun.

170
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,543
DDOLDDOL SUSPECTS SANGHYUN

171
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:44,005
First of all, I felt he woke up
way too early today.

172
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,969
-Where are you going?
-[Sanghyun] I'm going on a walk.

173
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:51,221
CLUE 1
SOLO WALK AT DAWN

174
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:54,933
[Ddolddol] Maybe he tried
to explore the area?

175
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:57,644
His vibe today is different
from how it was yesterday.

176
00:07:57,727 --> 00:08:01,773
Also, we found out about the Seeker today.

177
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:04,275
-He was unfazed.
-[Ddolddol] But he wasn't surprised.

178
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:08,029
[host] We will now begin
the first Seeker Vote.

179
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:12,242
[Ddolddol] You know how people
have gut feelings? It's just my hunch.

180
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:14,744
-All we can do is guess right now.
-[Ddolddol] Yes, that's right.

181
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:17,247
So, I think it could be Sanghyun.

182
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:20,417
[Jimin] Kim Ddolddol
was pretty convincing.

183
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,462
So more and more people
started to suspect Sanghyun.

184
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:25,922
That's fine too.

185
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:27,674
As long as I don't get eliminated.

186
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:28,758
SANGHYUN TALKS WITH A COP

187
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:29,968
What do you think?

188
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,302
I had some suspicions

189
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:33,179
-about Kim Ddolddol.
-[Sanghyun] I see.

190
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:34,264
[Eunsil] Or maybe Horseking?

191
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,474
How did Ddolddol contact you?

192
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:39,352
-He only sent you intel.
-By phone.

193
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:41,730
-Yes, he messaged me directly.
-By phone?

194
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:42,981
We got nothing from him.

195
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:44,941
It's because he's handsome.

196
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:47,360
-Is that why?
-[all laughing]

197
00:08:47,444 --> 00:08:48,528
He could be his type.

198
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:49,612
Am I unattractive?

199
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:52,532
No, I mean, he could be his type.

200
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,826
[Junseo] I don't know. It's just a hunch.

201
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:59,164
I'm being cautious about saying this.

202
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:02,375
It's just the impression
I get from people.

203
00:09:02,459 --> 00:09:04,002
But the Seeker has to...

204
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:06,671
SANGHYUN ENTERS DINING ROOM

205
00:09:06,755 --> 00:09:07,756
[Jieun] Right, right.

206
00:09:09,174 --> 00:09:10,216
Right, right.

207
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:13,595
[♪ tense music playing]

208
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,804
[Jieun sighs]

209
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:23,563
[Sanghyun] You know how something
just feels off about someone?

210
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:29,277
I'm curious. Is there only one Seeker?

211
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,361
Yes, one.

212
00:09:30,445 --> 00:09:31,654
Does it say that anywhere?

213
00:09:34,199 --> 00:09:35,533
I don't see it written anywhere.

214
00:09:35,617 --> 00:09:36,659
That's a new take.

215
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:40,330
THERE COULD BE TWO SEEKERS?

216
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:43,166
I'm just thinking there could be two.

217
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:49,339
SANGHYUN THROWS OUT HIS THEORY AND LEAVES

218
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,548
That's a new angle.

219
00:09:50,632 --> 00:09:52,175
-Two Seekers.
-[Ddolddol] Right.

220
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:57,263
That's when I was completely convinced

221
00:09:57,889 --> 00:09:59,182
that it was Sanghyun.

222
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:01,643
We only had to catch one person.

223
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,812
It felt like he was trying to distract us,

224
00:10:03,895 --> 00:10:06,606
so I headed straight to prison.

225
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:08,650
When the cops came here,

226
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,944
-did they say there might be two Seekers?
-No.

227
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,153
[Ddolddol] Well, they just told us.

228
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:13,488
-They didn't tell us.
-[Ddolddol] Sanghyun did.

229
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:15,907
In that case, it would split the votes.

230
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:16,991
[Joonsu] A distraction tactic?

231
00:10:17,075 --> 00:10:18,326
DDOLDDOL SUSPECTS SANGHYUN

232
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:19,994
When Ddolddol said that,

233
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,080
I thought, "He's right."

234
00:10:22,163 --> 00:10:25,291
Sanghyun is the one
I'm most suspicious of.

235
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:26,876
Kim Ddolddol

236
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:30,338
seems to have really good instincts.

237
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:33,591
Do we have to vote within an hour?

238
00:10:33,675 --> 00:10:35,218
That wasn't mentioned.

239
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:48,398
Earlier, I talked with Jaegyun
and Horseking here.

240
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:52,485
They seem to be
really suspicious of the cop team.

241
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:54,154
They're suspicious of the cop team?

242
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:56,698
[Jimin] Yes, because the Seeker
planned the whole game.

243
00:10:56,781 --> 00:11:00,618
But I feel like it can't be the cops.

244
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:04,873
The reason why I thought
there could be two Seekers is

245
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,332
Ddolddol...

246
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,584
Sorry.

247
00:11:08,168 --> 00:11:11,254
-[Jimin] What? What did you say?
-Mr. Ddolddol and Joonsu

248
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,672
kept talking to each other.

249
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:15,508
When we visited the prison earlier,
I went to get food,

250
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:16,843
and they were talking separately.

251
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,052
Everyone was at prison,

252
00:11:18,136 --> 00:11:20,680
but what did they need
to talk about in that situation?

253
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,182
DDOLDDOL & JOONSU TALK PRIVATELY

254
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:24,809
If there are two Seekers,
it could be those two.

255
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:26,227
That's what I thought.

256
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,605
But wouldn't that be unlikely,

257
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:31,024
considering how Ddolddol
betrayed Joonsu yesterday?

258
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:34,485
-Who knows? Maybe to win alone...
-But that could be part of his plan.

259
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:38,615
[Eunsil] Right, maybe the mission
was to sabotage his team.

260
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:40,575
[Sanghyun] I didn't know

261
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,411
that other people
were suspecting the cops though.

262
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:44,662
[Jaegyun] Very shady.

263
00:11:44,746 --> 00:11:47,415
EXCEPT FOR SANGHYUN,
ALL MALE PLAYERS HAVE VISITED THE PRISON

264
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,293
-[Joonsu] It's warm.
-[Jaegyun] It's warm as hell.

265
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:51,502
[Joonsu sighs]

266
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:53,630
[♪ contemplative music playing]

267
00:11:57,008 --> 00:12:00,011
Do you guys think
the Seeker is among the cops?

268
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,222
[Sanghyun] Hmm.

269
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,892
Do you think the Seeker
is a cop too, Jaegyun?

270
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,728
I do have that suspicion.

271
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:11,856
To me, this feels like nothing
but a witch hunt,

272
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:13,900
because the game
would become too easy then.

273
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:23,409
The more we talk about it,
the more confusing it gets.

274
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:27,288
[chuckles]

275
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,334
[Horseking] I can't decide.

276
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,336
-[Jaegyun] I have no idea.
-I really can't pick.

277
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:37,090
[Sanghyun] I don't know what happened,

278
00:12:37,173 --> 00:12:40,093
but Ddolddol must've been very persuasive.

279
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:44,264
It felt like everyone wanted me out.

280
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:53,273
Why is everyone doing this to me?

281
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:57,068
15 MINUTES BEFORE SEEKER VOTE

282
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:02,824
[Ddolddol] There wasn't much time left.

283
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:05,785
If I didn't do something,

284
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:09,205
it felt like the votes would be split.

285
00:13:09,289 --> 00:13:10,581
[ZZONE] Who is it?

286
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:11,874
[Ddolddol] Are the ladies all here?

287
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,251
[Jimin] Yes, you can come in.

288
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:17,213
[Ddolddol] I thought people who would be
easily swayed were there.

289
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:20,425
I needed to play politics
to get their votes.

290
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:21,676
So, here's the thing.

291
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:26,180
If Sanghyun is the Seeker,
we made the right choice for survival.

292
00:13:26,264 --> 00:13:27,932
But if he's not the Seeker,

293
00:13:28,016 --> 00:13:30,560
we'd feel bad,
and no one would vote him out.

294
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,980
The one the Seeker picked
should be eliminated.

295
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:38,109
FOUR PEOPLE SWAYED BY KIM DDOLDDOL

296
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:40,236
We have nothing to lose, right?

297
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:43,322
-It's the most reasonable choice.
-It is the most reasonable.

298
00:13:43,406 --> 00:13:44,657
He's the biggest threat,

299
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:47,493
so why would we keep him around?

300
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:48,911
Here's 80 million won

301
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:50,246
-in personal funds.
-Thank you.

302
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:51,414
REMOVE A WEALTHY RIVAL

303
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:54,417
-He's one step ahead.
-I know.

304
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:58,546
I think I got gaslit in that moment,
so I started thinking...

305
00:13:58,629 --> 00:14:00,298
"Maybe it really is Youn Sanghyun."

306
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,175
Maybe it's the right move strategically.

307
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,093
[Ddolddol] The women
were all nodding there.

308
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:05,970
I thought, "Okay, I convinced them."

309
00:14:06,054 --> 00:14:09,015
Then, I went to the room
where Jaegyun and Horseking were.

310
00:14:09,891 --> 00:14:12,351
Listen, this is what
I just told the women.

311
00:14:12,435 --> 00:14:14,687
-We need everyone on the same page.
-Right.

312
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:17,899
I spoke to him one-on-one just now
while looking at his eyes.

313
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:19,776
[Sanghyun] Do you think it's one person?

314
00:14:20,443 --> 00:14:21,944
I'm guessing there's only one.

315
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,447
Starting with two
would make the game too complicated.

316
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:26,657
That's true.

317
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:30,036
Maybe I'm biased,
because I'm fixated on him.

318
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:32,830
But I got the feeling
he was kind of smirking.

319
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:34,248
Plus, he's an actor,

320
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:37,418
so he's the only one
who can stay composed and put up a front.

321
00:14:37,502 --> 00:14:38,753
So, here's the thing.

322
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:41,589
If Sanghyun unfairly becomes
an elimination candidate,

323
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,175
people will vote
for someone else out of guilt.

324
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,593
Either way, Sanghyun survives.

325
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:48,096
Horseking and I were picked
first and second

326
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:49,472
-as Good Citizens.
-Right.

327
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:50,556
DDOLDDOL GATHERS VOTES

328
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,808
[mic feedback]

329
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:55,436
[host] We'll now begin the Seeker Vote.

330
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,647
Once you've made your decision,

331
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:00,191
please go to the Dealer Room
and cast your vote.

332
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:04,237
Hello.

333
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:07,532
[dealer] Please cast your vote
to identify the Seeker.

334
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:11,285
SEEKER VOTE
YOUN SANGHYUN

335
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:12,912
Sorry, Sanghyun.

336
00:15:13,538 --> 00:15:16,457
[Jaegyun] Since
we've gathered enough votes...

337
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:20,795
[Horseking] We should vote for Sanghyun
since it gives us a majority.

338
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:26,425
-[shivering]
-[♪ contemplative music playing]

339
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,809
[Pani Bottle] Damn,
it's tough now that I'm here.

340
00:15:37,145 --> 00:15:38,187
I'm sorry.

341
00:15:38,271 --> 00:15:40,940
I gave it some thought
and voted for ZZONE.

342
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:42,024
SEEKER VOTE
ZZONE

343
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:45,778
PANI BOTTLE VOTED FOR ZZONE

344
00:15:46,404 --> 00:15:47,738
Here's another option.

345
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:50,616
To survive the Death Match,
pick someone weaker.

346
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:52,493
That's the only option.

347
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:54,787
If you're not sure, pick ZZONE.

348
00:15:54,871 --> 00:15:56,747
Yeah, vote for ZZONE. Help us out.

349
00:15:57,832 --> 00:16:01,419
If you aren't sure, go with ZZONE
so we can survive the Death Match.

350
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:04,297
The Seeker will pick
a strong player for sure.

351
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,550
[Pani Bottle] Logically,
we should bring someone down

352
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:09,343
we might have a chance against.

353
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:11,679
We stopped looking for the Seeker.

354
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:14,056
I targeted ZZONE.

355
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,226
Let's be strategic and pick someone
we're most likely to beat.

356
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:19,478
SANGHYUN 3
DDOLDDOL, JAEGYUN, HORSEKING

357
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:21,230
ZZONE 3
PANI BOTTLE, SUJIN, DAIL

358
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:23,399
[host] The Seeker Vote has ended.

359
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,401
Please gather in the Main Hall.

360
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:26,694
[♪ tense music playing]

361
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,237
I guess someone's going to go down.

362
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:33,701
[mic feedback]

363
00:16:34,202 --> 00:16:36,871
[host] We will reveal the results
of the Seeker Vote.

364
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:42,251
[Ddolddol] A lot of people
were swayed by me.

365
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:44,086
I felt like I'd convinced them.

366
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:48,341
[ZZONE] I think the people in prison
were determined to go after me.

367
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,468
[Eunsil] I decided to go
with the majority.

368
00:16:51,052 --> 00:16:53,012
[Sanghyun] Since Ddolddol
started accusing me,

369
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,640
I thought people
would vote for me as the Seeker.

370
00:16:56,307 --> 00:16:59,393
[host] The player
who received the most votes is...

371
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:07,318
Kim Ddolddol.

372
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:12,990
I didn't expect that result at all.

373
00:17:13,074 --> 00:17:14,533
I was really shocked.

374
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:18,246
-[chuckles]
-[gasps]

375
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:24,919
[Ddolddol] Who on earth was it?

376
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,547
Was I stabbed in the back
by someone I trusted?

377
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,927
SILENCE FILLS THE MAIN HALL

378
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:42,144
[Sanghyun] If I'm in danger,
I might as well go after Ddolddol.

379
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:46,524
30 MINUTES AGO

380
00:17:48,651 --> 00:17:51,737
[Jieun] Right after Ddolddol left,
Sanghyun walked in.

381
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,448
What are you going to do?

382
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:58,077
To be honest,
when the four of us were talking earlier,

383
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,954
your name did come up.

384
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,330
Ddolddol's name came up too.

385
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:04,584
Because yesterday, Ddolddol deceived us.

386
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,752
[Sanghyun] With Ddolddol targeting me,

387
00:18:06,836 --> 00:18:08,045
it worked out in my favor.

388
00:18:08,129 --> 00:18:11,882
I could use public opinion
and muddy the waters a bit.

389
00:18:11,966 --> 00:18:14,802
When it came to the messages
Ddolddol sent me,

390
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:18,389
he was wrong about the part
that was causing confusion.

391
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,057
You mean the info he told you?

392
00:18:20,141 --> 00:18:21,934
It wasn't entirely correct.

393
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:23,060
So, here's the thing.

394
00:18:23,144 --> 00:18:26,188
He came all the way here
to create confusion.

395
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:30,735
Ddolddol lied the day before.

396
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,028
[host] Good Citizen.

397
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:33,321
DURING COPS AND ROBBERS

398
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:34,405
Kim Ddolddol.

399
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,781
KIM DDOLDDOL WAS THE TRAITOR

400
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:39,869
Let's compare the moment
when we got tricked and now.

401
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:42,538
Jieun said they felt similar.

402
00:18:42,622 --> 00:18:44,415
I agree with voting out Ddolddol

403
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:47,043
because he keeps doubting me.

404
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,336
-It should be him.
-Ddolddol?

405
00:18:48,419 --> 00:18:49,420
-Okay.
-Ddolddol.

406
00:18:49,503 --> 00:18:50,504
SETTLED ON DDOLDDOL

407
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:54,425
SEEKER VOTE
KIM DDOLDDOL

408
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:55,801
[chuckling]

409
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:03,559
[Sanghyun] I thought he was pretty smart,
but now I'm a bit disappointed.

410
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:06,020
[host] Also, here is the result
of the first Seeker Vote.

411
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:09,523
In terms of arresting the Seeker...

412
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,402
[Jieun] I wasn't completely sure,

413
00:19:13,486 --> 00:19:16,697
but I thought Ddolddol
was the most suspicious one.

414
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:20,326
[Eunsil] I thought
he was trying to frame Sanghyun

415
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,119
because he was the actual Seeker.

416
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:24,747
[Sanghyun] I wasn't sure. I really wasn't.

417
00:19:26,082 --> 00:19:27,625
[host] ...you have failed.

418
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,338
[Jimin] We're doomed.

419
00:19:34,215 --> 00:19:35,758
[Ddolddol] How can they be that slow?

420
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,426
I was so pissed off.

421
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:39,720
I was 100% sure it was Sanghyun.

422
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:43,974
[Sanghyun] Why did he have to target me

423
00:19:44,058 --> 00:19:46,936
when he wasn't even sure?

424
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:49,814
[ZZONE] I felt completely blindsided.

425
00:19:51,941 --> 00:19:53,984
[Eunsil] I was totally stunned.

426
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:58,114
If it's not Kim Ddolddol,
we have to vote again.

427
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,699
[host] Lastly,

428
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:02,993
we will reveal the elimination candidate
chosen by the Seeker.

429
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:06,706
LAST NIGHT

430
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:09,417
The Seeker Room has opened.

431
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:15,131
DEADLY TAG
RULES

432
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,800
[distorted voice] The person
I'd like to eliminate is...

433
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:21,387
THE ELIMINATION CANDIDATE
CHOSEN BY THE SEEKER IN ADVANCE

434
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:24,432
[host] Between Kim Ddolddol
and the person chosen by the Seeker,

435
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:26,517
the one who receives the most votes

436
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,019
will become
the final elimination candidate.

437
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:31,856
If the person chosen by the Seeker
is Kim Ddolddol,

438
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:33,816
Kim Ddolddol
will automatically be confirmed

439
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,068
as the elimination candidate
without a vote.

440
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:39,280
The elimination candidate
chosen by the Seeker is...

441
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,824
[Horseking] I feel like
the Seeker will choose me.

442
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,951
[Jaegyun] What if it ends up being me?

443
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:45,911
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

444
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,914
[host] The elimination candidate
chosen by the Seeker is...

445
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:55,421
Kim Ddolddol.

446
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:59,425
THE SEEKER PREDICTED
THE SEEKER VOTE RESULTS ACCURATELY

447
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:02,219
[♪ moody music playing]

448
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:09,685
[Ddolddol] Who's the Seeker?
I had to know who the Seeker was.

449
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:14,982
[host] Kim Ddolddol,
please leave the area immediately.

450
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,358
I really did my best.

451
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:20,446
-Well, it's not over yet.
-It's not over.

452
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:22,239
[sighs loudly]

453
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:31,624
I was sent straight to prison
without being an elimination candidate.

454
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:34,168
Why? Because it was
Kim Ddolddol versus Kim Ddolddol.

455
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:38,255
So I was the one who got the most votes
as the suspected Seeker.

456
00:21:38,339 --> 00:21:42,051
On top of that, I was also the one
the Seeker wanted to eliminate.

457
00:21:42,134 --> 00:21:43,844
Maybe I got too involved.

458
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:45,095
I kind of regret it.

459
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:50,142
THE MAIN HALL IS LEFT IN SHOCK

460
00:21:51,227 --> 00:21:52,853
How could they both be the same person?

461
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:55,105
That's epic.

462
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:59,151
-[Sujin laughs] Someone's coming.
-Here he comes.

463
00:21:59,235 --> 00:22:01,320
-[Sujin] My goodness!
-[Dail] Welcome!

464
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:03,155
-Mr. Ddolddol.
-[Pani Bottle] Excuse me.

465
00:22:03,239 --> 00:22:05,616
Please get changed.
We have rules here too.

466
00:22:05,699 --> 00:22:07,493
That's not the right attitude.

467
00:22:07,576 --> 00:22:09,745
-Is there some strict hierarchy here?
-[Sujin laughing]

468
00:22:10,538 --> 00:22:12,331
Hello, let me introduce myself.

469
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:16,252
What should I do first?
Maybe I should clean first.

470
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:18,712
-Want me to clean this up?
-[Sujin] No, it's fine.

471
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,300
I guess I'm the newbie here.

472
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:26,679
What can you do?
I better adjust quickly to prison life.

473
00:22:27,263 --> 00:22:28,305
I have to survive.

474
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:31,934
I'll survive, get back out there,
and find out who the Seeker is for sure.

475
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:34,228
[♪ serious music playing]

476
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:37,606
3:00 A.M.

477
00:22:45,573 --> 00:22:46,574
DEADLY TAG
RULES

478
00:22:46,657 --> 00:22:49,118
[host] Seeker, please select
the next elimination candidate.

479
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:53,455
[distorted voice] It was a perfect play.

480
00:22:57,710 --> 00:22:59,295
Ah. It was so thrilling.

481
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:02,882
[Eunsil sighs]

482
00:23:05,676 --> 00:23:06,677
-[Eunsil] So now...
-[Junseo] Mmm.

483
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,220
Are you confused?

484
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:10,431
I think it's Sanghyun.

485
00:23:12,975 --> 00:23:16,770
I hope I'm wrong,
but I also do feel that Sanghyun...

486
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:20,399
I'm suspicious of him.

487
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:23,027
What makes you think that?
Why do you suspect him?

488
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:24,862
They said there was a benefit

489
00:23:24,945 --> 00:23:28,574
that could give the Seeker
an advantage right from the start.

490
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:30,743
I think maybe it was about

491
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:33,287
choosing a team.

492
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,747
You and I became cops.

493
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:38,834
Then, it was obvious
that cops would have a huge advantage.

494
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:43,631
I actually had my suspicions all along
in the back of my mind.

495
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:45,758
Can I ask who you voted for?

496
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,885
[Jaegyun] To be honest,
it was Youn Sanghyun.

497
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:49,053
-For real?
-[Jaegyun] Yes.

498
00:23:49,595 --> 00:23:50,971
So we talked about it.

499
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:54,475
Ddolddol said if he was chosen
by the Seeker,

500
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:56,727
we should suspect Youn Sanghyun.

501
00:23:56,810 --> 00:24:00,189
And the Seeker really picked Ddolddol,
so that's when I thought,

502
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,315
"Wait a minute."

503
00:24:01,398 --> 00:24:03,734
[Pani Bottle] Who do you think
they'll vote for next?

504
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,361
[Ddolddol] I think they'll pick Sanghyun.

505
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:09,198
Wouldn't it be weird
not to suspect him at this point?

506
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:12,993
You openly accused Sanghyun,
and you ended up getting eliminated.

507
00:24:13,077 --> 00:24:17,706
So naturally, Sanghyun should be
the one everyone votes for next.

508
00:24:18,374 --> 00:24:19,875
SANGHYUN WILL LIKELY BE VOTED AS SEEKER

509
00:24:19,959 --> 00:24:22,252
I'm 99% certain that it's Sanghyun.

510
00:24:22,336 --> 00:24:24,630
[Pani Bottle] So no matter
who gets taken out among us,

511
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,507
let's vote for Sanghyun next round.

512
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:29,510
But if it's not him,
we're back to square one.

513
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:33,138
[Ddolddol] I think
we might build a bond this way.

514
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,016
[Pani Bottle] The problem is,
one of us has to be eliminated.

515
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,477
[Ddolddol] We developed a bond
we didn't have before.

516
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:42,564
We were determined to find a way back
and catch the Seeker no matter what.

517
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:45,651
Sanghyun,
you're not getting away with this.

518
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,486
[Jieun] Are you the Seeker?

519
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:49,947
It's not me.

520
00:24:50,531 --> 00:24:54,284
I realized I couldn't continue like this,
so I decided to get aggressive.

521
00:24:55,411 --> 00:24:57,663
Isn't this going exactly
how the Seeker wants?

522
00:24:57,746 --> 00:24:58,747
-[Jimin] Yes.
-[Jieun] Exactly.

523
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:00,124
The person the Seeker chose

524
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:02,543
-got voted out anyway.
-[ZZONE] The same person...

525
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:06,463
Then, is it among the six of us
who went after Kim Ddolddol?

526
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,507
It's possible. The odds are--

527
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:11,468
Would it have been necessary
to target Kim Ddolddol

528
00:25:11,552 --> 00:25:13,178
-as the Seeker?
-[Jieun] I thought about it.

529
00:25:13,262 --> 00:25:14,847
[ZZONE] There is a possibility.

530
00:25:14,930 --> 00:25:16,473
It might just be a coincidence.

531
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:18,392
[Sanghyun] When we happened
to accuse Kim Ddolddol,

532
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,436
-it's like, "This is perfect."
-[Jieun] Exactly.

533
00:25:20,519 --> 00:25:22,688
-They may have thought that.
-[Jieun] Yeah, we don't know that.

534
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:25,024
[Sanghyun] When we started leaning toward
voting for Ddolddol,

535
00:25:25,107 --> 00:25:27,901
Jimin did kind of take the lead.

536
00:25:28,485 --> 00:25:32,072
If we all agree on one person to vote for,

537
00:25:32,156 --> 00:25:33,699
that person will definitely be out.

538
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:35,117
Yeah, they'll definitely be out.

539
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,202
Then, how about we all vote
for the same person?

540
00:25:37,286 --> 00:25:39,955
The best option we have

541
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:41,832
is actually voting for Ddolddol.

542
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:43,333
JIMIN GAVE IDEA TO VOTE FOR DDOLDDOL

543
00:25:43,417 --> 00:25:44,918
He's the only one we can agree on.

544
00:25:45,002 --> 00:25:48,255
Because who else can we pick?
Sanghyun, ZZONE, or Joonsu?

545
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:50,507
-Okay, then Ddolddol?
-[Sanghyun] Ddolddol?

546
00:25:50,591 --> 00:25:51,925
I thought it worked out well.

547
00:25:52,009 --> 00:25:53,594
Let's make this useful.

548
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:56,305
Maybe I should steer people
toward Jimin as the Seeker.

549
00:25:56,889 --> 00:25:58,057
[sighs heavily]

550
00:25:58,807 --> 00:25:59,808
This is so stressful.

551
00:26:00,601 --> 00:26:01,602
[Junseo] Why?

552
00:26:03,187 --> 00:26:04,772
I'm suspicious of two people.

553
00:26:04,855 --> 00:26:05,856
[Junseo] Who?

554
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:08,025
[Sanghyun] Jimin and Jieun.

555
00:26:08,108 --> 00:26:09,359
[Junseo] Jimin and Jieun?

556
00:26:10,152 --> 00:26:11,153
Why?

557
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:12,863
[Sanghyun] There's something off
about them.

558
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:15,699
I feel like they're hiding something
when they talk.

559
00:26:15,783 --> 00:26:18,911
Whenever we try to figure out
who the Seeker is, it feels like...

560
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:21,038
they stop halfway.

561
00:26:21,121 --> 00:26:23,832
I don't know. It's just a gut feeling.

562
00:26:23,916 --> 00:26:24,917
Horseking.

563
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,001
SANGHYUN GOES TO HORSEKING

564
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:29,088
-Who do you think it is?
-[Horseking] Who? I'm not sure.

565
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:32,382
My gut tells me it's Jieun or Jimin.

566
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:34,426
With Jimin, it's not just a hunch.

567
00:26:34,510 --> 00:26:37,721
There are quite a few things
that made me suspicious of Jimin.

568
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:39,431
[Horseking] You think
she's playing politics?

569
00:26:39,515 --> 00:26:42,810
Yeah, I believe she's just really good
at playing the game.

570
00:26:42,893 --> 00:26:44,311
SANGHYUN STARTS TARGETING JIMIN

571
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:47,564
The one who was behind the idea
of going after Ddolddol

572
00:26:47,648 --> 00:26:49,608
was actually Jimin.

573
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:52,194
And to be fair, I was part of that too.

574
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:53,779
I agreed to go with Ddolddol

575
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:55,989
because he'd been suspicious of me.

576
00:26:56,073 --> 00:26:58,117
I thought I'd go after him as well.

577
00:26:58,659 --> 00:27:02,329
[Horseking] So Jimin took the lead?

578
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:06,166
It was a group decision,
but she was the one who picked him.

579
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:09,795
The upside of going with Jimin is
that she's influential,

580
00:27:09,878 --> 00:27:11,380
so it's worth looking into her.

581
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:13,507
[♪ suspicious music playing]

582
00:27:13,590 --> 00:27:17,594
JIMIN IS UNAWARE OF SANGHYUN'S SCHEME

583
00:27:24,935 --> 00:27:26,937
[Jimin] Sanghyun
seems so nervous right now,

584
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:29,439
which makes me think it might not be him.

585
00:27:29,523 --> 00:27:31,733
I do feel bad for Kim Ddolddol.

586
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:34,152
I feel guilty,
so I keep thinking about it.

587
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:39,950
But honestly, I thought
the prison uniform looked pretty cool,

588
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:41,827
so I kind of wanted to try it on.

589
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:42,911
[Sujin] Blue.

590
00:27:43,996 --> 00:27:45,372
[Sujin laughing]

591
00:27:46,081 --> 00:27:47,833
-[Pani Bottle] It looks good on you.
-Hello, everyone.

592
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:49,418
[Pani Bottle] What are you in for?

593
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:52,212
-[Ddolddol] I was falsely accused.
-[Pani Bottle] "Falsely accused."

594
00:27:52,296 --> 00:27:55,591
I have a cool undertone,
so blue looks great on me.

595
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,969
-It's mealtime.
-[Sujin] You can put it down there.

596
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,387
[Ddolddol] Everyone, the food is here.

597
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:02,389
-I'll bring it over for you.
-[Pani Bottle] You can leave it.

598
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:04,099
-[Sujin] Wait, the food...
-[Dail Kimchi and bean sprouts?

599
00:28:04,975 --> 00:28:06,602
-What?
-[Pani Bottle] Did we get less food?

600
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:11,064
[Ddolddol] They gave us kimchi
and bean sprouts for our meal.

601
00:28:11,148 --> 00:28:12,691
This is seriously bad.

602
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,319
I need to get out of the prison life fast.

603
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,571
I can't sleep with makeup on.

604
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:19,865
But I should just sleep.
Who cares about my skin?

605
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:22,117
-[Dail laughs]
-[Ddolddol] This is nice.

606
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:24,578
The sound of the water is like ASMR.

607
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,788
Am I made for prison life?

608
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:37,257
[Joonsu] What a nice day.

609
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:39,968
[♪ rock music playing]

610
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:48,268
[Sanghyun] What an interesting place.

611
00:28:48,352 --> 00:28:49,811
[Jaegyun exclaims]

612
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:51,980
[Horseking] This place is scary.

613
00:28:53,190 --> 00:28:54,775
-[ZZONE] Wow. Interesting.
-[Sanghyun] I know.

614
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:56,485
[ZZONE] This place is totally abandoned.

615
00:28:59,029 --> 00:29:01,365
[Jieun] I should lure people over here.

616
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:04,201
This place is unbelievable.

617
00:29:04,284 --> 00:29:06,411
[Junseo] There were a lot of structures.

618
00:29:06,495 --> 00:29:09,206
The first thing I noticed was

619
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:11,416
how surprisingly spacious it felt.

620
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:12,960
[Joonsu] The doors were ripped off,

621
00:29:13,710 --> 00:29:15,587
and the roof was covered in rust.

622
00:29:16,213 --> 00:29:17,381
It was kind of scary.

623
00:29:19,716 --> 00:29:21,093
[mic feedback]

624
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:23,929
[host] Welcome to the game area, everyone.

625
00:29:24,554 --> 00:29:27,975
We will reveal
the second Main Match of Deadly Tag.

626
00:29:28,058 --> 00:29:29,434
The second Main Match is...

627
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:32,604
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves."

628
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:37,734
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves"
is a nine-player game of cat and mouse

629
00:29:37,818 --> 00:29:42,030
in which the roles of hunter and prey
switch as time goes on.

630
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:45,909
There is a total
of three roles in this game.

631
00:29:45,993 --> 00:29:48,870
Dogs, Wolves, and Hunters.

632
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:52,082
Dogs can only tag other Dogs,

633
00:29:52,165 --> 00:29:53,959
receiving one point per tag.

634
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:57,838
A player tagged by a Dog loses one point.

635
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:01,466
Wolves can tag Dogs or Wolves,

636
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:04,428
receiving three points per tag.

637
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:07,681
A player tagged by a Wolf
loses three points.

638
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:12,019
Hunters can tag Dogs or Wolves,

639
00:30:12,102 --> 00:30:14,187
receiving two points per tag.

640
00:30:14,271 --> 00:30:17,232
A player tagged by a Hunter
loses two points.

641
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:22,612
The roles will vary depending on
who they can or cannot tag.

642
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:26,408
If a player incorrectly tags
someone they're not allowed to,

643
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:28,744
they will lose two points.

644
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:32,122
So, Dogs and Wolves
can't tag Hunters, right?

645
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:33,206
No.

646
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:34,666
[Joonsu] They're basically
invincible then.

647
00:30:34,750 --> 00:30:36,251
The Hunter is the best role.

648
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:40,088
[host] Before the game,
every player receives one Wolf marker

649
00:30:40,172 --> 00:30:42,215
and one Hunter marker.

650
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:44,968
They must place these markers

651
00:30:45,052 --> 00:30:48,138
on the six time slots
from Monday to Saturday.

652
00:30:49,306 --> 00:30:52,934
If a Wolf marker is placed on a time slot,
the player becomes a Wolf.

653
00:30:53,018 --> 00:30:56,063
A Hunter marker makes them a Hunter.

654
00:30:56,146 --> 00:30:58,065
And if there is no marker,

655
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:00,484
they become a Dog.

656
00:31:01,777 --> 00:31:05,989
Each day can have
a maximum of three players assigned.

657
00:31:06,073 --> 00:31:09,618
But on Wednesday, there is no limit
on the number of players.

658
00:31:09,701 --> 00:31:12,037
Should we all have a dogfight
with a Wolf on Wednesday?

659
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:14,581
I think I'd lose that fight,
so I won't mess around.

660
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:19,795
[host] Starting from the player
with the least amount of current funds,

661
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:23,173
players will enter in order
for the first round of placements.

662
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:27,010
The second round of placements
will be done in reverse order.

663
00:31:27,761 --> 00:31:31,098
The chase will last 15 minutes
for each day,

664
00:31:31,181 --> 00:31:33,141
and once the time runs out,

665
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:35,852
the game will automatically move on
to the next day.

666
00:31:36,937 --> 00:31:39,773
At this point, players' roles
will not be revealed,

667
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:42,734
and only the number
of Wolves and Hunters will be revealed.

668
00:31:43,401 --> 00:31:46,655
You don't know who's who,
so you can't just tag anyone.

669
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:47,906
If you tag the wrong person,

670
00:31:47,989 --> 00:31:49,116
-you'll lose points.
-[ZZONE] Right.

671
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:50,492
Gosh, this is tricky.

672
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:55,705
[host] Any player with a score of
minus 20 points or lower during the game

673
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:58,875
will be immediately eliminated.

674
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:01,920
The game will consist of two rounds.

675
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:05,924
The player with the highest score
at the end will be the winner,

676
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:07,926
receiving 20 million won in personal funds

677
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:10,554
and one Elimination Immunity Pass.

678
00:32:11,304 --> 00:32:14,516
On the other hand,
players with scores minus 20 or lower

679
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:16,101
will become elimination candidates.

680
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:19,396
They will choose two players
without Elimination Immunity Passes.

681
00:32:19,479 --> 00:32:22,607
Along with one player
selected through an Elimination Vote,

682
00:32:22,691 --> 00:32:24,734
they'll enter a Death Match.

683
00:32:25,735 --> 00:32:28,363
I think it'll all come down
to where you're placed.

684
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:31,366
If you choose Hunter

685
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,034
and there are three Hunters,

686
00:32:33,118 --> 00:32:34,202
it's over.

687
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:37,914
If you're the only Hunter,
you're invincible and can tag anyone.

688
00:32:37,998 --> 00:32:40,000
You have to be careful.

689
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:41,501
It's a battle of wits.

690
00:32:43,128 --> 00:32:46,339
[Jieun] I think good liars could have
an advantage.

691
00:32:46,423 --> 00:32:48,508
[Joonsu] Even if I'm just a Dog,

692
00:32:48,592 --> 00:32:51,636
if I act bold and approach a Hunter,

693
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:54,931
they might think I'm a Hunter
and get scared.

694
00:32:55,015 --> 00:32:58,143
[ZZONE] I think the key
will be to psych people out.

695
00:32:59,144 --> 00:33:01,313
[host] The chase area
consists of two zones,

696
00:33:01,396 --> 00:33:04,900
the Residential Area
and the Factory Complex.

697
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:09,112
The Residential Area has open spaces,

698
00:33:09,196 --> 00:33:11,990
making it easier to chase or run away.

699
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:17,329
The factory complex has
buildings and obstacles,

700
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:19,956
making it easy to hide or ambush others.

701
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:23,335
Next, here's how the tag system works.

702
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:27,839
At the start of the game,
each player gets one patch.

703
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:33,428
If you stick it on another player's back,
the tag is successful.

704
00:33:33,511 --> 00:33:34,596
Sorry about that.

705
00:33:35,222 --> 00:33:37,015
-You stick them on.
-[Joonsu] You tag them.

706
00:33:37,098 --> 00:33:38,683
It'll be easier than ripping it off.

707
00:33:38,767 --> 00:33:40,393
Yeah, it's much easier to stick them on.

708
00:33:40,477 --> 00:33:43,355
[host] Also,
you cannot tag the same player

709
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:45,482
more than once on the same day.

710
00:33:47,525 --> 00:33:51,780
You'll now have 30 minutes
for private discussions.

711
00:33:52,948 --> 00:33:53,949
ROUND 1 PRIVATE TALKS

712
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:56,117
Does the Seeker still have
a mission during this too?

713
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:58,662
-We have to identify their mission, right?
-[Jaegyun] Yeah.

714
00:34:01,748 --> 00:34:06,628
THE SEEKER STILL REMAINS A MYSTERY

715
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:08,421
Can an alliance even work here?

716
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:11,174
If someone lies within the alliance,
you're done for.

717
00:34:11,258 --> 00:34:12,801
Exactly. The Seeker's role is

718
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:15,679
to sabotage the game
so no one ends up winning.

719
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:17,555
The Seeker's role could be big today.

720
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:18,682
Yeah, totally.

721
00:34:18,765 --> 00:34:21,017
An alliance with the Seeker
will likely lead to losing,

722
00:34:21,101 --> 00:34:23,103
because they'll prevent you from winning.

723
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:26,481
I think Sanghyun is my number one suspect

724
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:27,691
-as the Seeker.
-Yeah.

725
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:28,984
[Jaegyun laughs]

726
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:31,611
If you team up with him,
you'll be in big trouble today.

727
00:34:32,445 --> 00:34:34,114
Then, vote me out.

728
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:36,866
-Seriously, just vote me out.
-I'll handle it. I got it.

729
00:34:36,950 --> 00:34:39,244
-Why do you keep saying that? I get it.
-[Jieun] I'm testing you.

730
00:34:39,327 --> 00:34:40,954
[Sanghyun] How many times will you say it?

731
00:34:41,037 --> 00:34:43,164
Don't cry. Don't cry, don't cry.

732
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:49,462
[Sanghyun] She's been accusing me
as the Seeker since yesterday.

733
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:51,548
[Jieun] Are you the Seeker?

734
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:52,966
[Eunsil] I think it's Sanghyun.

735
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,175
It seems like it's Sanghyun.

736
00:34:54,259 --> 00:34:57,512
UNDER SUSPICION SINCE LAST NIGHT

737
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,015
[Sanghyun] It felt like everyone
was suspicious of me.

738
00:35:01,516 --> 00:35:03,977
So I felt kind of...

739
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,648
bitter and lonely.

740
00:35:12,652 --> 00:35:15,322
I think I might play
on my own for this game.

741
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:17,657
No, if you team up,
you're guaranteed to win.

742
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,619
Team up? How?

743
00:35:20,702 --> 00:35:22,829
For example, [whispers]

744
00:35:23,538 --> 00:35:25,123
you'll have to lie a little.

745
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:27,292
Let's say I'm a Wolf on Friday,

746
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:28,460
but you tell everyone

747
00:35:29,294 --> 00:35:31,379
that you think I'm a Dog.

748
00:35:32,464 --> 00:35:33,715
[Jimin] I figured

749
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:36,551
if a Hunter reveals on their own
when they're playing,

750
00:35:36,635 --> 00:35:39,846
I'd be able to figure things out.

751
00:35:39,929 --> 00:35:41,890
So I made a proposal to Eunsil.

752
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:44,559
And I wanted to team up with Yuk Junseo.

753
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:49,481
Because his competitiveness,
speed, and stamina

754
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,399
would be very helpful to me.

755
00:35:51,483 --> 00:35:52,484
So I wrote him a note.

756
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:55,153
TEAMING UP WILL GIVE US AN ADVANTAGE
LET'S WORK TOGETHER

757
00:35:57,781 --> 00:35:58,782
Junseo, can you go

758
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:00,283
-ask for water?
-Sorry?

759
00:36:00,367 --> 00:36:02,369
-Water? What water?
-Can you get some water?

760
00:36:02,452 --> 00:36:03,828
-Drinking water.
-For drinking?

761
00:36:03,912 --> 00:36:06,539
You go ask them since you look scary.

762
00:36:06,623 --> 00:36:09,125
[laughing] She makes people
who look strong do errands.

763
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:11,252
Hey.

764
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:13,088
Where did he go?

765
00:36:13,171 --> 00:36:14,589
Where is he?

766
00:36:14,673 --> 00:36:15,799
PRETENDING TO SEARCH

767
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,175
You have to ask... Hey.

768
00:36:17,258 --> 00:36:20,470
AND PASSES HIM THE NOTE

769
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:22,222
Could we get some water?

770
00:36:26,184 --> 00:36:28,061
[Eunsil] What's your plan, Junseo?

771
00:36:29,104 --> 00:36:32,148
Your offer was very nice,

772
00:36:32,232 --> 00:36:33,650
but I'll go solo for now.

773
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:37,153
Since the Seeker has a mission
to create confusion,

774
00:36:37,237 --> 00:36:40,407
I thought teaming up with others
could be risky.

775
00:36:41,366 --> 00:36:43,410
[Jimin] I can't team up with Junseo then.

776
00:36:44,244 --> 00:36:45,412
What do I do?

777
00:36:47,831 --> 00:36:48,915
What about you?

778
00:36:48,998 --> 00:36:51,167
We still don't have anything concrete.

779
00:36:51,251 --> 00:36:53,920
I don't trust anyone enough
to share information either.

780
00:36:54,003 --> 00:36:56,589
Of course, because you can't
show anything clearly.

781
00:36:56,673 --> 00:36:59,926
There are conditions within the rules,
so I can't really trust anyone.

782
00:37:00,510 --> 00:37:02,137
I thought about it over and over,

783
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,930
but I couldn't trust anyone.

784
00:37:04,013 --> 00:37:06,266
I wasn't sure who I should team up with.

785
00:37:06,349 --> 00:37:08,309
Everyone seemed suspicious.

786
00:37:10,437 --> 00:37:11,438
Seriously,

787
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:14,232
this is so hard.

788
00:37:15,275 --> 00:37:16,651
It's not easy.

789
00:37:16,735 --> 00:37:18,778
Whenever I suggested teaming up,

790
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:22,907
everyone seemed as if they would be
the ones losing out.

791
00:37:26,286 --> 00:37:30,457
But that's when I started thinking.

792
00:37:31,291 --> 00:37:34,085
Maybe I should actually use
this situation to my advantage.

793
00:37:39,424 --> 00:37:40,925
-[ZZONE] Joonsu.
-[Joonsu] Yes?

794
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:43,595
What are you going to do?

795
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:45,096
[in English] Ladies first.

796
00:37:45,180 --> 00:37:46,931
-[in Korean] Well...
-[Joonsu] Did you decide to team up?

797
00:37:47,015 --> 00:37:49,726
Team up? No. No one's teaming up.
Everyone's on their own.

798
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:50,977
Come over here.

799
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:54,314
So basically,

800
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:57,150
-we just need to avoid coming in last.
-[ZZONE] Right.

801
00:37:57,233 --> 00:37:58,860
How about we don't tag each other?

802
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:01,529
-And no voting each other out.
-[ZZONE] Sounds good.

803
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:02,947
Then, should we go with that?

804
00:38:03,031 --> 00:38:04,616
[ZZONE] To be honest,

805
00:38:04,699 --> 00:38:06,868
anyone could easily tag me

806
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:08,995
because everyone's strong physically.

807
00:38:09,078 --> 00:38:11,331
I needed to find someone to team up with.

808
00:38:11,915 --> 00:38:14,209
-[Jieun] ZZONE.
-This won't do. I shouldn't try to fight.

809
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:16,461
-Can you not go after me?
-[ZZONE] Me?

810
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:17,712
Aren't you going to tag me?

811
00:38:17,796 --> 00:38:19,547
Tag you? I'm not planning to.

812
00:38:19,631 --> 00:38:22,008
-I'm scared.
-Me too. Same here.

813
00:38:22,592 --> 00:38:26,638
It looked like Jieun and Joonsu
were thinking about forming an alliance.

814
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:29,390
It was actually an alliance
of the weakest.

815
00:38:29,474 --> 00:38:30,725
-When you...
-[ZZONE] Let's have a chat.

816
00:38:30,809 --> 00:38:32,519
When you're the Hunter,

817
00:38:32,602 --> 00:38:35,146
if you tag her, you get three points.

818
00:38:35,897 --> 00:38:37,482
-Wait, that's minus points.
-Wait, no.

819
00:38:37,565 --> 00:38:39,234
-That's minus points.
-No.

820
00:38:39,317 --> 00:38:41,486
There's three of us,
and we each get a day as a Hunter.

821
00:38:41,569 --> 00:38:43,321
We won't know who else is a Hunter,

822
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:45,198
but we'll know one of us will be one.

823
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:47,200
The others won't know
which one is a Hunter.

824
00:38:47,283 --> 00:38:50,495
If each of us takes a day,
one of us will be a Hunter half the time.

825
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:51,788
Then, Hunters...

826
00:38:52,372 --> 00:38:53,748
[Joonsu] Since we're weaker players,

827
00:38:53,832 --> 00:38:56,584
instead of putting all our Hunters
and Wolves on the same day,

828
00:38:56,668 --> 00:38:57,919
we decided to spread them out.

829
00:38:58,002 --> 00:38:59,754
One of us becomes a Wolf on Monday,

830
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:02,674
and another person becomes
a Hunter on Tuesday.

831
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:05,009
Our strategy was to protect each other.

832
00:39:05,093 --> 00:39:06,761
If someone comes and tries to tag us,

833
00:39:07,512 --> 00:39:10,014
since one of us is a Hunter,

834
00:39:10,098 --> 00:39:11,182
the Hunter can stop them.

835
00:39:11,266 --> 00:39:13,142
They don't know who it is,
so what can they do?

836
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:16,020
As a group of three,
we won't be alone. Do you get it?

837
00:39:16,104 --> 00:39:17,605
Then, we won't have to hide as much.

838
00:39:17,689 --> 00:39:18,857
[ZZONE] Looking back,

839
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:21,609
since we're the ones at the bottom,
we had less funds

840
00:39:21,693 --> 00:39:24,195
and were the first ones
who could place our markers.

841
00:39:24,279 --> 00:39:26,239
The remaining spots
were three sets of three,

842
00:39:26,322 --> 00:39:30,159
so we were in a position to get
a rough idea of how they'd be placed.

843
00:39:30,243 --> 00:39:31,870
I thought it could work in our favor.

844
00:39:31,953 --> 00:39:32,954
I'll go with Saturday. [whispering]

845
00:39:33,037 --> 00:39:34,038
ALLIANCE'S PLACEMENT PLAN

846
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:35,957
-I'll take Monday too.
-[Jieun] I'll do this day.

847
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:37,041
I'll do Monday.

848
00:39:37,125 --> 00:39:39,252
-[Jieun] I'll take this one.
-It's the most risky one.

849
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:40,712
We'd be almost invincible.

850
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:43,006
Isn't this a guaranteed win?

851
00:39:44,215 --> 00:39:46,759
It feels like
we have a pretty decent chance.

852
00:39:46,843 --> 00:39:48,928
One of us might get in
the top tier in rankings.

853
00:39:50,013 --> 00:39:54,642
[host] Round 1 marker placements
will begin now.

854
00:39:54,726 --> 00:39:56,853
-[♪ exciting music playing]
-Jaegyun and Sanghyun.

855
00:39:58,354 --> 00:39:59,772
HORSEKING

856
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:01,900
Do wolves usually have
different-colored eyes?

857
00:40:01,983 --> 00:40:03,234
They're like Siberian Huskies.

858
00:40:03,318 --> 00:40:05,320
It's heterochromia.
Different-colored eyes.

859
00:40:05,403 --> 00:40:07,572
That's how they are when you look at them.

860
00:40:08,740 --> 00:40:10,199
ROUND 1
MARKER PLACEMENT

861
00:40:10,283 --> 00:40:11,451
Should I be a Hunter?

862
00:40:11,534 --> 00:40:12,535
ZZONE GOES FIRST

863
00:40:12,994 --> 00:40:14,162
Hunter, Wolf.

864
00:40:14,871 --> 00:40:16,664
Hunter. Wolf.

865
00:40:21,502 --> 00:40:22,754
[gasps]

866
00:40:23,963 --> 00:40:27,300
PLACEMENT ROOM

867
00:40:27,383 --> 00:40:29,469
Hello. [gasps]

868
00:40:29,552 --> 00:40:30,929
MON, TUE, WED, THU, FRI, SAT

869
00:40:31,012 --> 00:40:33,389
[dealer] Ms. ZZONE,
place your marker on the board.

870
00:40:34,057 --> 00:40:35,099
I'll go with this.

871
00:40:35,683 --> 00:40:38,937
You've placed
the Hunter marker on Saturday.

872
00:40:39,020 --> 00:40:43,691
MARKER PLACEMENT RULE: ONLY ONE HUNTER
OR WOLF MARKER CAN BE PLACED AT A TIME

873
00:40:43,775 --> 00:40:45,360
[Joonsu] This is scary.

874
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:46,903
LEE JOONSU IS SECOND

875
00:40:46,986 --> 00:40:49,656
[dealer] Mr. Lee Joonsu,
place your marker on the board.

876
00:40:49,739 --> 00:40:51,032
EARLIER PLACEMENTS ARE HIDDEN

877
00:40:51,115 --> 00:40:53,242
I'll place the Hunter marker on Thursday.

878
00:40:53,326 --> 00:40:55,870
You've placed
the Hunter marker on Thursday.

879
00:40:56,913 --> 00:41:00,750
Ms. Shin Jieun,
place your marker on the board.

880
00:41:00,833 --> 00:41:02,001
[Jieun] Really?

881
00:41:06,089 --> 00:41:07,256
In that case...

882
00:41:07,966 --> 00:41:10,176
[Joonsu] We agreed on the days
we'd each place our markers on,

883
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:13,012
but I was really worried
that Jieun might betray us.

884
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:15,306
I'll go with this.

885
00:41:15,974 --> 00:41:18,726
[dealer] You've placed the Wolf marker
on Wednesday.

886
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:39,956
MARKER PLACEMENT CONTINUES

887
00:41:44,085 --> 00:41:46,254
[host] Marker placement is complete.

888
00:41:52,552 --> 00:41:54,929
[footsteps approaching]

889
00:41:58,808 --> 00:42:00,059
[distorted voice] Am I...

890
00:42:00,560 --> 00:42:02,145
meant to be the spy?

891
00:42:04,105 --> 00:42:06,691
[dealer] We will designate the goal
for the Seeker mission.

892
00:42:06,774 --> 00:42:08,693
Please name two players.

893
00:42:13,531 --> 00:42:14,824
Shin Jieun

894
00:42:15,783 --> 00:42:17,577
and Hwang Jaegyun.

895
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:22,331
I wonder how fun today's going to be.

896
00:42:23,833 --> 00:42:29,130
THE SEEKER IS STILL ON THE MOVE

897
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:33,176
[host] Round 1's chase will begin shortly.

898
00:42:33,634 --> 00:42:35,470
Please head to each of your positions.

899
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:39,974
-[♪ exciting music playing]
-It's so spacious. It's really big.

900
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:44,312
I need to figure out
my strategy for this area.

901
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:46,481
If there are one Hunter

902
00:42:47,148 --> 00:42:49,776
and two Wolves,

903
00:42:49,859 --> 00:42:51,194
that'd be the best.

904
00:42:51,277 --> 00:42:53,404
[host] Once the marker placements
are revealed,

905
00:42:53,488 --> 00:42:55,114
the round will begin.

906
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,331
[Jimin] There are two Wolves
and two Hunters?

907
00:43:03,414 --> 00:43:05,708
[♪ contemplative music playing]

908
00:43:06,626 --> 00:43:08,377
[Jaegyun] They said
there'd be three in total.

909
00:43:09,670 --> 00:43:11,339
They clearly said

910
00:43:11,422 --> 00:43:13,341
there'd be three in each slot.

911
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:17,011
[host] Each day can have
a maximum of three players assigned.

912
00:43:17,095 --> 00:43:20,389
But on Wednesday, there is no limit
on the number of players.

913
00:43:21,057 --> 00:43:22,183
I tried to place

914
00:43:22,266 --> 00:43:25,061
my Hunter marker on Monday,
but I heard it was full.

915
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,562
MONDAY

916
00:43:26,646 --> 00:43:29,357
[dealer] Monday already has
three markers in place,

917
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:30,817
so you cannot place another one.

918
00:43:32,652 --> 00:43:35,613
But it showed two Wolves and two Hunters,

919
00:43:35,696 --> 00:43:38,074
so I didn't understand what was going on.

920
00:43:38,157 --> 00:43:40,118
I knew right away that something was off.

921
00:43:43,830 --> 00:43:46,415
[alarm blaring]

922
00:43:51,838 --> 00:43:53,840
[host] Monday has begun.

923
00:43:59,804 --> 00:44:01,764
JANG EUNSIL

924
00:44:01,848 --> 00:44:04,100
On Monday, my role was a Dog.

925
00:44:04,183 --> 00:44:06,394
I took some tarp to make a tent...

926
00:44:09,814 --> 00:44:11,858
and hid right from the start.

927
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:14,569
I wanted to peek through

928
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:16,028
and see who came by.

929
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:21,325
PARK JIMIN

930
00:44:21,409 --> 00:44:24,829
I'm not someone
who can overpower others physically.

931
00:44:24,912 --> 00:44:27,957
So I figured I'd better hide
and stay safe.

932
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,460
DEFENSIVE STRATEGIES FOR DOGS

933
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:35,173
YOUN SANGHYUN

934
00:44:35,256 --> 00:44:36,424
It's a dead end.

935
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:39,093
[♪ exciting music playing]

936
00:44:39,177 --> 00:44:42,805
SANGHYUN SEARCHES FOR PREY

937
00:44:43,764 --> 00:44:45,391
JANG EUNSIL

938
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:46,684
I have to tag someone.

939
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:51,856
[Eunsil] That scared me.

940
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,609
MUYEONG FACTORY

941
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:55,735
[Sanghyun] Gosh, I'm beat.

942
00:45:00,281 --> 00:45:01,741
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

943
00:45:06,954 --> 00:45:07,955
Where are they?

944
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,972
[Jimin] There were a lot of places
to hide there.

945
00:45:25,056 --> 00:45:26,766
It was such a relief.

946
00:45:26,849 --> 00:45:28,684
I decided to hold out a little longer.

947
00:45:28,768 --> 00:45:31,145
[♪ rock music playing]

948
00:45:34,190 --> 00:45:35,900
[Joonsu] ZZONE, come with me.

949
00:45:35,983 --> 00:45:38,236
Let's go together.

950
00:45:38,319 --> 00:45:40,738
[Joonsu] I met up with ZZONE as planned.

951
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:42,698
If someone comes and tries to tag us,

952
00:45:42,782 --> 00:45:45,368
they don't know who it is,
so what can they do? Say, "Tag me."

953
00:45:45,451 --> 00:45:46,869
Then, we won't have to hide as much.

954
00:45:46,953 --> 00:45:48,037
THE ALLIES HIDE THEIR ROLES

955
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:50,790
ZZONE, LEE JOONSU

956
00:45:53,542 --> 00:45:54,627
Hang on.

957
00:45:54,710 --> 00:45:55,795
Hang on, hang on.

958
00:45:58,547 --> 00:45:59,548
Someone's here.

959
00:45:59,632 --> 00:46:01,634
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

960
00:46:04,553 --> 00:46:05,763
I'll cover your back.

961
00:46:05,846 --> 00:46:06,889
I'll watch our backs.

962
00:46:12,144 --> 00:46:13,145
It's Jaegyun.

963
00:46:14,021 --> 00:46:16,607
THEY RUN INTO HWANG JAEGYUN

964
00:46:18,192 --> 00:46:20,486
[ZZONE] We ended up running into Jaegyun
from the start.

965
00:46:20,569 --> 00:46:22,446
He's the most athletic out of everyone.

966
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:24,198
SHIN JIEUN

967
00:46:24,282 --> 00:46:26,993
[Jieun] On Monday, I was a Dog,
so I wanted to quickly reunite

968
00:46:27,076 --> 00:46:29,120
with ZZONE and Joonsu.

969
00:46:32,832 --> 00:46:34,125
RUNS INTO HORSEKING

970
00:46:34,208 --> 00:46:36,377
-What are you?
-Me?

971
00:46:37,253 --> 00:46:41,924
Of all people, the first person
I ran into was one of the strongest.

972
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:45,761
[Joonsu] What are you?

973
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,181
[Jaegyun laughs] Hey.

974
00:46:49,682 --> 00:46:51,142
Are you a Hunter?

975
00:46:55,229 --> 00:46:56,230
No.

976
00:46:56,314 --> 00:46:58,774
Even if I'm a Dog, I should act fearless.

977
00:46:58,858 --> 00:47:00,568
Then, they won't come after me,

978
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:03,237
because they'll mistake me
for a Wolf or Hunter.

979
00:47:14,707 --> 00:47:16,542
[host] Tag confirmed.

980
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:18,336
[Jaegyun] Ah, so you two are Hunters.

981
00:47:18,419 --> 00:47:19,628
JOONSU TAGS JAEGYUN

982
00:47:19,712 --> 00:47:21,255
He came charging in confidently,

983
00:47:21,339 --> 00:47:23,799
so I ran away
because I assumed he was a Wolf or Hunter.

984
00:47:24,508 --> 00:47:26,469
-What are you?
-Me?

985
00:47:26,552 --> 00:47:27,553
Are you a Hunter?

986
00:47:27,636 --> 00:47:29,764
I am... a Hunter.

987
00:47:30,348 --> 00:47:31,390
-You're a Hunter?
-Yes.

988
00:47:31,474 --> 00:47:32,767
HORSEKING, SHIN JIEUN

989
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:36,812
They don't know if I'm a Dog,
a Wolf, or a Hunter.

990
00:47:36,896 --> 00:47:39,482
I thought I should pretend to be a Hunter.

991
00:47:40,441 --> 00:47:41,901
-What do you want?
-Hold on.

992
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:44,070
Wait, what are you? Are you a Hunter?

993
00:47:44,153 --> 00:47:45,237
-What are you?
-What?

994
00:47:45,321 --> 00:47:46,947
-What are you?
-I can't tell you.

995
00:47:47,031 --> 00:47:48,699
-I told you mine.
-What are you doing?

996
00:47:48,783 --> 00:47:49,909
HORSEKING IS THE REAL HUNTER

997
00:47:49,992 --> 00:47:51,035
[Horseking] You're a Hunter?

998
00:47:51,118 --> 00:47:52,453
JIEUN INSISTS SHE'S A HUNTER

999
00:47:52,536 --> 00:47:53,788
You shouldn't come close then.

1000
00:47:55,956 --> 00:47:57,291
[Jieun] The funny thing is,

1001
00:47:57,375 --> 00:47:59,919
I was chasing Horseking

1002
00:48:00,002 --> 00:48:02,671
and he kept running away.

1003
00:48:06,092 --> 00:48:09,929
I felt like things were more in my favor
than I expected.

1004
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:13,140
With this strategy, I think I can avoid
being in last place.

1005
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:15,768
Hunter.

1006
00:48:15,851 --> 00:48:16,894
So Jieun is a Hunter.

1007
00:48:16,977 --> 00:48:17,978
A CONFUSED HUNTER

1008
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:19,063
Jieun is a Hunter?

1009
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:20,189
That doesn't add up.

1010
00:48:21,065 --> 00:48:23,442
[alarm blaring]

1011
00:48:24,276 --> 00:48:25,986
[host] Tuesday has begun.

1012
00:48:27,613 --> 00:48:29,073
[Jaegyun] You're dead meat, Joonsu.

1013
00:48:32,368 --> 00:48:35,955
HWANG JAEGYUN

1014
00:48:36,038 --> 00:48:38,165
I got tagged by Joonsu.

1015
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:39,583
JOONSU TAGGED JAEGYUN ON MONDAY

1016
00:48:39,667 --> 00:48:40,668
I got you.

1017
00:48:40,751 --> 00:48:42,711
I needed to get that punk at least once.

1018
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:50,052
SPOTS JOONSU

1019
00:48:53,556 --> 00:48:55,349
[panting]

1020
00:48:56,225 --> 00:48:58,102
I was a Dog that day.

1021
00:48:58,185 --> 00:48:59,812
but I ran to Jaegyun.

1022
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:01,272
[Joonsu] Want to exchange information?

1023
00:49:01,355 --> 00:49:02,648
-What?
-[Joonsu] Want to share info?

1024
00:49:02,731 --> 00:49:04,775
-You tagged me.
-[Joonsu] I'll leave this here and talk.

1025
00:49:04,859 --> 00:49:06,193
You tagged me once.

1026
00:49:07,319 --> 00:49:09,071
Do you want to share information?

1027
00:49:09,697 --> 00:49:11,282
Want to catch the Seeker with me?

1028
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:12,908
-What do you want?
-Leave it here?

1029
00:49:12,992 --> 00:49:13,993
Leave it there for now.

1030
00:49:14,618 --> 00:49:15,786
-I'm tossing it away.
-Okay.

1031
00:49:16,829 --> 00:49:17,913
Back up.

1032
00:49:17,997 --> 00:49:19,081
-What is it?
-Back up.

1033
00:49:19,165 --> 00:49:20,249
Do you have any information?

1034
00:49:21,208 --> 00:49:22,460
I'm a Hunter.

1035
00:49:22,543 --> 00:49:23,544
Right now?

1036
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:25,838
LEE JOONSU, HWANG JAEGYUN

1037
00:49:25,921 --> 00:49:26,922
You're lying.

1038
00:49:28,632 --> 00:49:30,676
-I'm not. It's true.
-[Joonsu] You're not a Hunter.

1039
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:31,927
Hey, you made the offer.

1040
00:49:33,053 --> 00:49:34,180
You put it on? Let's go.

1041
00:49:35,723 --> 00:49:38,017
-Why do you keep following me?
-[Joonsu] Sorry.

1042
00:49:38,100 --> 00:49:40,227
[Jaegyun] Hey, Joonsu tagged me twice.

1043
00:49:49,904 --> 00:49:50,905
Where's Joonsu?

1044
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:53,824
Hey, Joonsu!

1045
00:49:54,575 --> 00:49:55,576
Where did he go?

1046
00:49:57,036 --> 00:49:59,205
-I have a patch on my back, right?
-No.

1047
00:49:59,288 --> 00:50:00,581
NO PATCH WAS TAGGED ON HIM

1048
00:50:01,749 --> 00:50:03,042
Joonsu, you're dead meat.

1049
00:50:17,556 --> 00:50:19,767
[Joonsu] I was still a Dog,

1050
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:22,811
so I acted bold and confident again.

1051
00:50:22,895 --> 00:50:24,146
I was going to tag him,

1052
00:50:24,980 --> 00:50:27,066
but something felt different from earlier.

1053
00:50:27,149 --> 00:50:28,526
I felt something had changed.

1054
00:50:28,609 --> 00:50:30,236
I figured he wasn't a Dog,

1055
00:50:30,319 --> 00:50:32,488
so I walked up with my bare hands

1056
00:50:32,571 --> 00:50:33,906
and tapped him on the back.

1057
00:50:33,989 --> 00:50:36,367
I can be a bit sly.

1058
00:50:36,992 --> 00:50:39,286
I just couldn't believe it at all.

1059
00:50:39,370 --> 00:50:41,789
I got blindsided by a kid
who's not even 20 yet.

1060
00:50:41,872 --> 00:50:43,290
I felt so betrayed.

1061
00:50:48,295 --> 00:50:49,421
I can't believe Joonsu.

1062
00:50:49,505 --> 00:50:51,215
[panting]

1063
00:50:53,842 --> 00:50:56,720
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1064
00:50:58,180 --> 00:51:03,477
LEE JOONSU

1065
00:51:25,082 --> 00:51:26,083
[Jaegyun] Joonsu!

1066
00:51:30,671 --> 00:51:32,631
[Joonsu] ZZONE!

1067
00:51:41,473 --> 00:51:43,350
[Jaegyun] Geez, this punk's good
at running away!

1068
00:51:44,059 --> 00:51:45,227
Hey, hey!

1069
00:51:47,146 --> 00:51:48,272
[Jaegyun sighs]

1070
00:51:53,652 --> 00:51:57,615
JAEGYUN FAILS AGAIN TO GET REVENGE

1071
00:51:57,698 --> 00:52:00,576
-[alarm blaring]
-[host] Wednesday has begun.

1072
00:52:06,373 --> 00:52:07,791
[panting]

1073
00:52:11,211 --> 00:52:12,838
[Sanghyun] I was a Dog on Wednesday,

1074
00:52:12,921 --> 00:52:15,090
so I have to stay hidden for now.

1075
00:52:15,174 --> 00:52:16,175
YOUN SANGHYUN

1076
00:52:20,179 --> 00:52:21,263
HORSEKING TAGS JAEGYUN

1077
00:52:21,347 --> 00:52:22,348
JUNSEO TAGS JIEUN

1078
00:52:22,431 --> 00:52:24,183
The messages popped up on my phone.

1079
00:52:24,266 --> 00:52:25,726
I was really shocked.

1080
00:52:26,310 --> 00:52:28,228
Tags were happening so fast.

1081
00:52:28,729 --> 00:52:29,772
Things are crazy now.

1082
00:52:30,481 --> 00:52:31,815
It's a party.

1083
00:52:32,608 --> 00:52:33,609
HORSEKING

1084
00:52:33,692 --> 00:52:35,444
[Horseking] Once I became a Wolf
on Wednesday,

1085
00:52:35,527 --> 00:52:37,529
I wanted to tag every single one of them!

1086
00:52:40,949 --> 00:52:41,950
HORSEKING TAGS ZZONE

1087
00:52:42,034 --> 00:52:43,035
[host] Tag confirmed.

1088
00:52:43,118 --> 00:52:44,662
Go ahead and run if you can.

1089
00:52:45,537 --> 00:52:46,580
I'll tag you all.

1090
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:48,999
YUK JUNSEO

1091
00:52:49,083 --> 00:52:50,626
[Junseo] I was a Hunter on Wednesday.

1092
00:52:50,709 --> 00:52:53,879
My goal was to tag
every single person I saw.

1093
00:52:56,048 --> 00:52:57,299
-[Jaegyun] Spare me just this once.
-[Junseo] What?

1094
00:52:57,383 --> 00:52:58,384
JAEGYUN'S LOST IN THE MAZE

1095
00:52:58,467 --> 00:52:59,843
-[Jaegyun] Spare me.
-[Junseo] Sorry.

1096
00:53:00,552 --> 00:53:01,553
[host] Tag confirmed.

1097
00:53:01,637 --> 00:53:02,680
JUNSEO TAGS JAEGYUN

1098
00:53:02,763 --> 00:53:03,764
Tag confirmed.

1099
00:53:03,847 --> 00:53:05,557
HORSEKING TAGS JIEUN
JUNSEO TAGS ZZONE

1100
00:53:05,641 --> 00:53:06,767
Tag confirmed.

1101
00:53:06,850 --> 00:53:07,851
-Sorry.
-It's okay.

1102
00:53:07,935 --> 00:53:08,936
What on earth?

1103
00:53:09,728 --> 00:53:11,689
Are these fools
just playing without thinking?

1104
00:53:14,233 --> 00:53:15,651
[host] Tag confirmed.

1105
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:16,735
JUNSEO TAGS JOONSU

1106
00:53:17,403 --> 00:53:19,405
[dealer] Please retrieve your patches.

1107
00:53:20,239 --> 00:53:23,992
[Junseo] I'd tagged almost everyone,
and I was pretty exhausted.

1108
00:53:24,076 --> 00:53:25,077
SUPPLY STATION

1109
00:53:25,160 --> 00:53:26,161
[ZZONE] You can't do this.

1110
00:53:26,245 --> 00:53:28,330
[Horseking] There's no point
in tagging me.

1111
00:53:28,414 --> 00:53:29,581
[Jieun] How come?

1112
00:53:29,665 --> 00:53:30,916
Are you trying to tag first place?

1113
00:53:30,999 --> 00:53:32,751
Yes, I need to get more points.

1114
00:53:33,001 --> 00:53:34,002
[Horseking] That's...

1115
00:53:34,086 --> 00:53:35,212
[♪ intense music playing]

1116
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:36,755
[Junseo] I spotted Horseking,

1117
00:53:37,423 --> 00:53:38,799
so I decided to tag him.

1118
00:53:38,882 --> 00:53:39,883
JUNSEO CHASES HORSEKING

1119
00:53:54,606 --> 00:53:55,899
[Junseo pants]

1120
00:53:58,485 --> 00:53:59,987
[Horseking] I'll never get caught.

1121
00:54:01,405 --> 00:54:02,781
DID I GET AWAY?

1122
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:09,079
[sighs heavily] He's so relentless.

1123
00:54:16,211 --> 00:54:18,630
HORSEKING RUNS FOR HIS LIFE

1124
00:54:19,590 --> 00:54:22,009
JUNSEO KEEPS CHASING HORSEKING

1125
00:54:25,262 --> 00:54:26,263
[sighs]

1126
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:28,599
It was scary when he was chasing me.

1127
00:54:30,809 --> 00:54:32,019
GIVES UP IN THE END

1128
00:54:32,102 --> 00:54:33,395
-Are you a Wolf?
-[Junseo] What?

1129
00:54:33,479 --> 00:54:34,563
[Horseking] Are you a Wolf?

1130
00:54:34,646 --> 00:54:36,774
JUNSEO TAGS HORSEKING

1131
00:54:36,857 --> 00:54:37,900
I'm out of breath.

1132
00:54:37,983 --> 00:54:38,984
This is too damn hard.

1133
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:42,154
Geez.

1134
00:54:42,237 --> 00:54:44,239
I wanted to get away, but I was exhausted

1135
00:54:44,323 --> 00:54:45,616
"HE TAGGED MANY THAT DAY"

1136
00:54:45,699 --> 00:54:47,242
from all the running.

1137
00:54:49,203 --> 00:54:50,704
I couldn't keep going.

1138
00:54:51,914 --> 00:54:53,874
MUYEONG STORE

1139
00:54:54,666 --> 00:54:56,126
[Eunsil] I think Junseo is the top player.

1140
00:54:56,210 --> 00:54:57,211
[Joonsu] Really?

1141
00:54:57,294 --> 00:54:59,213
I keep getting alerts on my phone.

1142
00:54:59,296 --> 00:55:00,339
-For real?
-Yeah.

1143
00:55:01,173 --> 00:55:02,174
[Joonsu] You're right.

1144
00:55:02,257 --> 00:55:03,300
JUNSEO TAGS FIVE PLAYERS

1145
00:55:03,383 --> 00:55:04,885
-[Eunsil] So...
-[Joonsu] Why is he so good?

1146
00:55:04,968 --> 00:55:06,970
[Horseking] I'm so beat. [pants]

1147
00:55:12,017 --> 00:55:13,602
Junseo is totally out ahead.

1148
00:55:15,395 --> 00:55:18,607
I realized he had created a huge lead.

1149
00:55:18,690 --> 00:55:19,691
[sighs]

1150
00:55:19,775 --> 00:55:21,568
It didn't work out the way I planned.

1151
00:55:22,444 --> 00:55:24,738
I thought I had this game in the bag,

1152
00:55:24,821 --> 00:55:26,782
but I let my guard down.

1153
00:55:27,324 --> 00:55:31,328
YUK JUNSEO

1154
00:55:36,124 --> 00:55:37,918
[Jimin panting] Geez,
I'm so bad at running.

1155
00:55:38,001 --> 00:55:39,086
I can't handle this.

1156
00:55:40,546 --> 00:55:43,799
PARK JIMIN
NO TAGS

1157
00:55:43,882 --> 00:55:45,926
I had no idea what to do at that point.

1158
00:55:46,635 --> 00:55:48,804
My alliance plan didn't work out.

1159
00:55:48,887 --> 00:55:50,055
Your offer was very nice,

1160
00:55:50,138 --> 00:55:51,348
but I'll go solo for now.

1161
00:55:51,431 --> 00:55:54,268
I think I might play
on my own for this game.

1162
00:55:54,893 --> 00:55:56,562
[Jimin] I can't really run well.

1163
00:55:57,312 --> 00:55:58,355
I'm so exhausted.

1164
00:55:58,438 --> 00:56:00,399
INN

1165
00:56:00,482 --> 00:56:05,237
I realized this was a game
that put me at a disadvantage.

1166
00:56:05,320 --> 00:56:07,990
I had no idea
how I was going to get through this.

1167
00:56:09,908 --> 00:56:12,327
INCINERATOR

1168
00:56:14,788 --> 00:56:15,789
[exclaims]

1169
00:56:16,707 --> 00:56:19,001
JIMIN RUNS INTO JUNSEO

1170
00:56:20,294 --> 00:56:22,045
There's someone over there. Please.

1171
00:56:24,047 --> 00:56:25,048
JUNSEO TAGS JIMIN

1172
00:56:25,132 --> 00:56:27,217
[host] Tag confirmed.

1173
00:56:27,301 --> 00:56:28,302
[Junseo] Sorry.

1174
00:56:29,386 --> 00:56:31,680
[both panting heavily]

1175
00:56:41,231 --> 00:56:42,899
Could you please check my score?

1176
00:56:42,983 --> 00:56:44,860
MARKER PLACEMENT AND SCORES
CAN BE CHECKED HERE

1177
00:56:44,943 --> 00:56:46,528
Mr. Yuk Junseo, your score is six points.

1178
00:56:48,822 --> 00:56:49,906
[Junseo] Geez.

1179
00:56:50,449 --> 00:56:52,242
I tagged Jimin

1180
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:53,994
but I lost points.

1181
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:55,621
How did this happen?

1182
00:56:55,704 --> 00:56:57,247
I was really flustered.

1183
00:56:58,665 --> 00:56:59,666
Where is everyone?

1184
00:57:03,837 --> 00:57:06,173
GIGGLING

1185
00:57:06,256 --> 00:57:08,550
My strategy was to fake them out.

1186
00:57:08,634 --> 00:57:10,052
My plan was to get tagged

1187
00:57:10,135 --> 00:57:11,928
as much as I could when I was a Hunter.

1188
00:57:13,221 --> 00:57:16,016
[dealer] You've placed the Hunter marker
on Wednesday.

1189
00:57:16,683 --> 00:57:18,685
I figured there would be

1190
00:57:18,769 --> 00:57:21,396
a lot of reckless tagging in this game.

1191
00:57:21,480 --> 00:57:24,733
If that happened,
it would lead to a lot of negative points.

1192
00:57:24,816 --> 00:57:28,528
So, maybe the person
with the fewest negative points

1193
00:57:28,612 --> 00:57:30,280
could end up winning.

1194
00:57:30,364 --> 00:57:32,783
PARK JIMIN

1195
00:57:35,243 --> 00:57:36,328
[host] Tag confirmed.

1196
00:57:36,411 --> 00:57:37,412
SANGHYUN TAGS JIMIN

1197
00:57:37,496 --> 00:57:39,873
I was like,
"Please tag me, please tag me,"

1198
00:57:39,956 --> 00:57:41,625
so I kept taunting them.

1199
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:44,002
I got tagged so many times.

1200
00:57:44,086 --> 00:57:46,338
No, hold on.

1201
00:57:46,421 --> 00:57:47,422
[host] Tag confirmed.

1202
00:57:47,506 --> 00:57:48,507
ZZONE TAGS JIMIN

1203
00:57:49,257 --> 00:57:51,051
[Jimin] What? Wait.

1204
00:57:51,134 --> 00:57:52,219
Wait, Joonsu.

1205
00:57:52,302 --> 00:57:54,262
[host] Tag confirmed.

1206
00:57:54,346 --> 00:57:55,347
JOONSU TAGS JIMIN

1207
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:58,392
They'll end up losing points,

1208
00:57:58,475 --> 00:58:00,686
so my strategy paid off.

1209
00:58:05,941 --> 00:58:07,275
[alarm blaring]

1210
00:58:08,276 --> 00:58:10,404
[host] Thursday has begun.

1211
00:58:20,622 --> 00:58:22,040
I'm a Wolf on Friday though.

1212
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:25,711
MUYEONG FACTORY

1213
00:58:25,794 --> 00:58:26,837
[Sanghyun] Jimin.

1214
00:58:26,920 --> 00:58:28,130
I need to talk to you.

1215
00:58:28,213 --> 00:58:29,756
From Monday to Thursday,

1216
00:58:29,840 --> 00:58:31,925
a total of nine people have been Wolves.

1217
00:58:33,135 --> 00:58:34,469
What are you talking about?

1218
00:58:34,553 --> 00:58:36,471
Check the text again.

1219
00:58:36,555 --> 00:58:37,973
Just once.

1220
00:58:38,056 --> 00:58:39,891
There have been nine Wolves, right?

1221
00:58:39,975 --> 00:58:42,519
CHECKING THE CHAT NOTIFYING ROLES

1222
00:58:42,602 --> 00:58:44,312
I've never been a Wolf yet,

1223
00:58:44,396 --> 00:58:46,857
but it already shows nine Wolves.

1224
00:58:46,940 --> 00:58:50,360
I analyzed how many Wolves
and Hunters had appeared.

1225
00:58:50,444 --> 00:58:54,614
I was trying to figure out
what Friday would be like

1226
00:58:54,698 --> 00:58:56,032
and prepare for the game.

1227
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:57,325
But I got confused

1228
00:58:57,409 --> 00:59:00,370
when I realized
that there'd been nine wolves by Thursday.

1229
00:59:00,454 --> 00:59:01,621
-Three. Right.
-Three.

1230
00:59:01,705 --> 00:59:03,039
-Seven. Nine.
-Yes. Eight.

1231
00:59:03,123 --> 00:59:04,124
And mine is left.

1232
00:59:04,207 --> 00:59:05,375
JAEGYUN HASN'T BEEN A WOLF EITHER

1233
00:59:05,459 --> 00:59:06,460
But that's 10.

1234
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:09,463
Each slot could only hold
three roles from the start.

1235
00:59:09,546 --> 00:59:10,630
-Right?
-[Jaegyun] Yeah.

1236
00:59:11,339 --> 00:59:13,675
Let's find out who played
as a Wolf on which day.

1237
00:59:13,759 --> 00:59:15,177
[Jieun] Let's look into it.

1238
00:59:15,260 --> 00:59:17,012
-[Jaegyun] After the first round.
-[Jieun] Okay.

1239
00:59:18,680 --> 00:59:19,973
[Junseo] What is going on?

1240
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:21,224
The Wolf count was off.

1241
00:59:21,308 --> 00:59:24,561
I wondered why there were extra Wolves.

1242
00:59:24,644 --> 00:59:26,563
I was very suspicious.

1243
00:59:33,069 --> 00:59:35,322
[host] Friday has begun.

1244
00:59:36,782 --> 00:59:38,116
[Jieun screams]

1245
00:59:40,911 --> 00:59:43,580
[Eunsil] It's Friday,
so there isn't much time left.

1246
00:59:46,374 --> 00:59:47,876
[Jieun screams]

1247
00:59:47,959 --> 00:59:49,127
No!

1248
00:59:49,211 --> 00:59:50,212
EUNSIL TAGS JIEUN

1249
00:59:50,295 --> 00:59:51,463
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Tagged.

1250
00:59:51,546 --> 00:59:52,798
YOUN SANGHYUN

1251
00:59:52,881 --> 00:59:54,758
I was a Wolf on Friday.

1252
00:59:54,841 --> 00:59:56,384
I needed to hurry up.

1253
00:59:59,638 --> 01:00:00,639
SANGHYUN TAGS JIEUN

1254
01:00:00,722 --> 01:00:02,599
[host] Tag confirmed.

1255
01:00:03,266 --> 01:00:05,477
[Jimin] I was a Dog on Friday,
so I had to hide.

1256
01:00:06,520 --> 01:00:08,396
[Junseo] I stayed hidden
almost the whole time.

1257
01:00:10,524 --> 01:00:11,525
JOONSU TAGS EUNSIL

1258
01:00:11,608 --> 01:00:13,068
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-[Joonsu] I got you.

1259
01:00:16,196 --> 01:00:17,197
[Jaegyun] Hey.

1260
01:00:17,280 --> 01:00:18,281
Hey!

1261
01:00:18,365 --> 01:00:19,366
Hey, Eunsil.

1262
01:00:19,449 --> 01:00:20,742
You can't use wrestling on me!

1263
01:00:20,826 --> 01:00:22,035
Wait, this is cheating.

1264
01:00:22,828 --> 01:00:25,997
MUYEONG TOWN HALL

1265
01:00:26,581 --> 01:00:28,792
PLACEMENT ROOM

1266
01:00:29,876 --> 01:00:31,253
[dealer] Hello, Ms. ZZONE.

1267
01:00:31,336 --> 01:00:34,047
-I'd like to check my score.
-[dealer] We will check Ms. ZZONE's score.

1268
01:00:34,631 --> 01:00:36,925
Your score is negative 19 points.

1269
01:00:38,552 --> 01:00:39,636
[gasps]

1270
01:00:41,137 --> 01:00:44,057
I actually got tagged so many times.

1271
01:00:44,140 --> 01:00:46,977
I was supposed to hide,
but I couldn't find a spot.

1272
01:00:47,060 --> 01:00:48,436
ZZONE WAS TARGETED BY PREDATORS

1273
01:00:48,520 --> 01:00:49,521
Wait.

1274
01:00:50,689 --> 01:00:55,443
One of the people
I had teamed up with was a Wolf.

1275
01:00:55,527 --> 01:00:58,196
JOONSU WAS A WOLF ON WEDNESDAY

1276
01:01:01,491 --> 01:01:02,534
[ZZONE yelps]

1277
01:01:03,493 --> 01:01:05,078
I have to tag them now.

1278
01:01:05,161 --> 01:01:06,538
JOONSU WAS A HUNTER ON THURSDAY

1279
01:01:08,081 --> 01:01:09,374
THEY WERE TARGETED AS A GROUP

1280
01:01:09,457 --> 01:01:10,876
Wait!

1281
01:01:10,959 --> 01:01:12,335
-[Eunsil] I got her.
-[ZZONE] Wait...

1282
01:01:13,044 --> 01:01:15,922
They tried to stay together with me
but I kept getting tagged.

1283
01:01:16,006 --> 01:01:18,091
That's when I lost a bunch of points.

1284
01:01:21,219 --> 01:01:22,387
PLOPS DOWN

1285
01:01:23,847 --> 01:01:25,348
I have no idea what to do.

1286
01:01:29,644 --> 01:01:32,856
Do I take the gamble or not?

1287
01:01:39,154 --> 01:01:40,447
I got minus 19 points.

1288
01:01:40,530 --> 01:01:42,991
I'm headed to the Death Match.
Seriously, I'm a candidate!

1289
01:01:43,074 --> 01:01:44,993
Seriously, I'm not lying!

1290
01:01:45,076 --> 01:01:46,328
Wait, I swear. Listen.

1291
01:01:46,411 --> 01:01:48,538
I'm going to the Death Match.
I got minus 19.

1292
01:01:48,622 --> 01:01:50,081
-What?
-[ZZONE] If I go under minus 20,

1293
01:01:50,498 --> 01:01:52,125
I'll head to the Death Match and pick you.

1294
01:01:52,208 --> 01:01:54,002
-[Eunsil] How can I trust you?
-Let's go now

1295
01:01:54,085 --> 01:01:55,337
-and check my score.
-[Eunsil] Are you sure?

1296
01:01:55,420 --> 01:01:57,631
-I'm not good at math.
-[ZZONE] Do the math. I swear.

1297
01:01:57,714 --> 01:01:58,715
Do the math.

1298
01:01:59,341 --> 01:02:00,800
Look at how many times I got tagged.

1299
01:02:00,884 --> 01:02:03,303
-I got tagged eight times.
-I'll believe you.

1300
01:02:03,386 --> 01:02:05,847
[ZZONE] I mean, I don't care,
but I'll go vote right away.

1301
01:02:05,931 --> 01:02:07,057
[Eunsil] Okay.

1302
01:02:07,140 --> 01:02:09,434
So that's why you were just sitting here.

1303
01:02:09,517 --> 01:02:10,685
I've got nothing to lose.

1304
01:02:11,186 --> 01:02:13,146
[ZZONE] I was in danger
of finishing dead last.

1305
01:02:13,229 --> 01:02:16,358
I decided to act bold and go,
"If I get tagged, then so be it."

1306
01:02:16,441 --> 01:02:18,610
I chose to push through with confidence.

1307
01:02:19,986 --> 01:02:21,071
[Sanghyun] Are you done?

1308
01:02:21,154 --> 01:02:24,324
I'm at minus 19, so if you tag me,
let's be elimination candidates.

1309
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:28,036
-Is that so?
-Tag me, and I'll take you with me.

1310
01:02:28,119 --> 01:02:30,246
Not me. I'm absolutely rooting for you.

1311
01:02:30,330 --> 01:02:31,331
HANDSHAKE

1312
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:33,208
-Hey, be careful.
-I'm always on your side.

1313
01:02:33,291 --> 01:02:34,459
Tag me.

1314
01:02:35,377 --> 01:02:36,836
He ran away from me.

1315
01:02:37,587 --> 01:02:39,339
This isn't as bad for me as I thought.

1316
01:02:39,422 --> 01:02:41,049
I'm at minus 19 points.

1317
01:02:41,549 --> 01:02:42,717
Then, can I tag you?

1318
01:02:42,801 --> 01:02:45,303
If you want to go to the Death Match,
be my guest.

1319
01:02:45,387 --> 01:02:46,554
[scoffs]

1320
01:02:46,638 --> 01:02:48,473
Then, I'll automatically vote for you.

1321
01:02:49,057 --> 01:02:50,350
RUNS OFF

1322
01:02:52,060 --> 01:02:55,105
-Me? Want to be up for elimination?
-I have no choice. No.

1323
01:02:55,188 --> 01:02:57,190
Seriously, I'll pick you.
I'll really pick you.

1324
01:02:57,273 --> 01:02:58,733
[Horseking] You've come to terms with it?

1325
01:02:58,817 --> 01:03:00,944
-Yes.
-Okay, embrace it. I'll give you that.

1326
01:03:01,027 --> 01:03:02,529
When will you be a Hunter?

1327
01:03:02,612 --> 01:03:03,863
-Saturday.
-[Jieun] Saturday?

1328
01:03:03,947 --> 01:03:05,615
-Okay. You'll give it a shot then?
-Yeah.

1329
01:03:05,699 --> 01:03:07,367
I need to give it a shot on Saturday.

1330
01:03:07,450 --> 01:03:08,868
PLANNING TO GO FOR IT ON SATURDAY

1331
01:03:08,952 --> 01:03:10,036
I was so anxious.

1332
01:03:10,120 --> 01:03:11,830
GNAWING ON HER PEN

1333
01:03:12,455 --> 01:03:15,458
I figured I just had to
hold out until Saturday

1334
01:03:15,542 --> 01:03:17,585
to turn things around.

1335
01:03:18,253 --> 01:03:19,963
I'll push through to the end.

1336
01:03:21,548 --> 01:03:23,425
[host] Saturday has begun.

1337
01:03:24,592 --> 01:03:25,927
ZZONE IS SATURDAY'S LONE HUNTER

1338
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:34,853
There's no one here.

1339
01:03:40,150 --> 01:03:41,192
Let's check.

1340
01:03:49,826 --> 01:03:50,827
PARK JIMIN

1341
01:03:50,910 --> 01:03:53,413
[Jimin] I was a Wolf on Saturday,
but I laid low.

1342
01:03:53,496 --> 01:03:55,915
It's because my goal
was to avoid being last.

1343
01:03:55,999 --> 01:03:57,917
-And there's ZZONE.
-I'm at minus 19 points.

1344
01:03:58,001 --> 01:04:00,253
If you want to go to the Death Match,
be my guest.

1345
01:04:00,336 --> 01:04:01,463
ZZONE REVEALED SHE'S LAST

1346
01:04:01,546 --> 01:04:03,590
That's when I decided to stay hidden.

1347
01:04:04,299 --> 01:04:06,676
They managed to hide so well.

1348
01:04:06,760 --> 01:04:09,596
I couldn't find them anywhere.
They disappeared completely.

1349
01:04:09,679 --> 01:04:11,556
I'm going to the Death Match.
I got minus 19.

1350
01:04:11,639 --> 01:04:13,183
I'm really at minus 19 points.

1351
01:04:13,266 --> 01:04:15,143
WITH A LIKELY ELIMINATION CANDIDATE

1352
01:04:15,226 --> 01:04:21,107
THE PLAYERS GO INTO HIDING

1353
01:04:21,858 --> 01:04:23,902
I thought it was a good strategy,

1354
01:04:24,611 --> 01:04:26,738
but it turned out to be
a double-edged sword.

1355
01:04:27,447 --> 01:04:29,699
I felt so helpless and frustrated.

1356
01:04:46,841 --> 01:04:47,842
[Junseo] What are you doing?

1357
01:04:48,968 --> 01:04:51,346
-Oh. Junseo. [chuckles]
-What are you doing?

1358
01:04:52,472 --> 01:04:54,182
-I'll tag you.
-[Sanghyun] I missed you.

1359
01:04:54,265 --> 01:04:56,101
-Why? Are you a Hunter?
-No.

1360
01:04:56,810 --> 01:04:58,228
[Sanghyun] No tagging this time.

1361
01:04:58,311 --> 01:04:59,562
How does that sound?

1362
01:04:59,646 --> 01:05:00,647
Deal?

1363
01:05:01,523 --> 01:05:02,941
I won't tag you.

1364
01:05:03,024 --> 01:05:05,735
-I ran so much. Since yesterday.
-[Sanghyun] How long have you been here?

1365
01:05:05,819 --> 01:05:06,903
Since yesterday?

1366
01:05:06,986 --> 01:05:07,987
That's a long time.

1367
01:05:10,031 --> 01:05:11,491
[Jieun] You need to tag just anyone.

1368
01:05:11,574 --> 01:05:12,575
I need to tag someone.

1369
01:05:14,494 --> 01:05:16,204
I kept running around,

1370
01:05:16,871 --> 01:05:18,623
but I couldn't find anyone at all.

1371
01:05:28,800 --> 01:05:31,010
[alarm blaring]

1372
01:05:33,888 --> 01:05:34,973
[sighs, grunts]

1373
01:05:39,602 --> 01:05:41,020
I felt terrible.

1374
01:05:43,189 --> 01:05:45,024
[host] Round 1 is over.

1375
01:05:47,735 --> 01:05:49,154
Before moving on to Round 2,

1376
01:05:49,237 --> 01:05:51,114
we will announce the current rankings.

1377
01:05:51,698 --> 01:05:52,699
In third place,

1378
01:05:52,782 --> 01:05:54,033
Youn Sanghyun.

1379
01:05:55,368 --> 01:05:56,619
In second place,

1380
01:05:56,703 --> 01:05:57,996
Yuk Junseo.

1381
01:05:59,539 --> 01:06:01,791
-Who's first place?
-[host] In first place,

1382
01:06:01,875 --> 01:06:02,959
Horseking.

1383
01:06:04,586 --> 01:06:06,421
1ST HORSEKING
2ND JUNSEO, 3RD SANGHYUN

1384
01:06:06,504 --> 01:06:07,505
8TH ZZONE, JIEUN

1385
01:06:07,589 --> 01:06:09,382
Junseo.

1386
01:06:09,465 --> 01:06:10,925
In terms of tags,

1387
01:06:11,009 --> 01:06:12,552
don't you have seven or eight?

1388
01:06:12,635 --> 01:06:13,636
ROUND 2 PRIVATE TALKS

1389
01:06:13,720 --> 01:06:15,346
I had some wrong tags.

1390
01:06:15,889 --> 01:06:18,725
LOST 4 POINTS FROM 2 WRONG TAGS

1391
01:06:18,808 --> 01:06:20,018
What?

1392
01:06:20,977 --> 01:06:23,897
TOTAL 8 TAGS
2 WRONG TAGS

1393
01:06:24,564 --> 01:06:26,691
[Horseking] I was going to
tag everyone at first,

1394
01:06:26,774 --> 01:06:29,027
but I changed my plans in the middle.

1395
01:06:29,110 --> 01:06:31,654
I decided to only tag
the people I was sure about

1396
01:06:31,738 --> 01:06:33,781
and secure points.

1397
01:06:34,490 --> 01:06:35,867
You can tag me.

1398
01:06:35,950 --> 01:06:37,118
Please tag me.

1399
01:06:37,202 --> 01:06:38,369
AVOIDS SUSPICIOUS PLAYERS

1400
01:06:39,162 --> 01:06:40,455
TAGS ONLY THE SURE TARGETS

1401
01:06:40,538 --> 01:06:41,539
No.

1402
01:06:43,583 --> 01:06:46,252
TOTAL 6 TAGS
0 WRONG TAGS

1403
01:06:46,336 --> 01:06:48,171
Three, three.

1404
01:06:48,254 --> 01:06:50,924
AND THIRD PLACE YOUN SANGHYUN

1405
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:52,550
Seven, eight, nine.

1406
01:06:53,551 --> 01:06:54,761
I was in third place,

1407
01:06:54,844 --> 01:06:56,304
but I couldn't relax.

1408
01:06:56,387 --> 01:06:57,430
[♪ contemplative music playing]

1409
01:06:57,513 --> 01:07:01,184
It's because I was the prime suspect
for being the Seeker.

1410
01:07:01,267 --> 01:07:02,268
In fact,

1411
01:07:02,894 --> 01:07:05,271
if you don't come in first place,
it's meaningless.

1412
01:07:05,355 --> 01:07:07,148
You need to get
an Elimination Immunity Pass

1413
01:07:07,232 --> 01:07:09,275
to stay out of the vote.

1414
01:07:10,443 --> 01:07:13,738
To me, aside from voting,

1415
01:07:13,821 --> 01:07:16,532
I'm still suspicious of him.

1416
01:07:16,616 --> 01:07:18,534
I think Sanghyun is the one.

1417
01:07:20,119 --> 01:07:21,120
[Jaegyun] Youn Sanghyun...

1418
01:07:27,377 --> 01:07:29,254
[Dail] I wonder
what kind of chase they're doing.

1419
01:07:30,964 --> 01:07:33,424
[Pani Bottle] The next vote
will mostly likely be against Sanghyun.

1420
01:07:33,508 --> 01:07:34,717
He'll be voted out.

1421
01:07:34,801 --> 01:07:36,094
[Pani Bottle] They should all suspect him.

1422
01:07:36,177 --> 01:07:37,178
Right.

1423
01:07:37,262 --> 01:07:39,931
If Sanghyun isn't the Seeker,
I think we're screwed.

1424
01:07:40,932 --> 01:07:42,475
It has to be him.

1425
01:07:43,184 --> 01:07:46,145
But if it's not Sanghyun,
the Seeker must be thrilled now.

1426
01:07:46,229 --> 01:07:48,231
They're not even on anyone's radar.

1427
01:07:48,314 --> 01:07:50,775
And everyone's turning on each other.

1428
01:07:50,858 --> 01:07:53,152
-It's the best-case scenario.
-[Sujin] It's a great situation.

1429
01:07:56,614 --> 01:07:59,450
[Sanghyun] I had to finish in first
and get the Elimination Immunity Pass.

1430
01:08:00,326 --> 01:08:02,120
I had to solve

1431
01:08:02,620 --> 01:08:04,789
the mystery of the Wolf count.

1432
01:08:05,581 --> 01:08:06,958
There's something going on.

1433
01:08:10,920 --> 01:08:12,171
When were you a Wolf?

1434
01:08:12,255 --> 01:08:13,298
[ZZONE] On Thursday.

1435
01:08:13,381 --> 01:08:14,632
Was there anything strange?

1436
01:08:14,716 --> 01:08:15,758
-[ZZONE] Strange?
-Yeah.

1437
01:08:15,842 --> 01:08:17,677
-The Wolves...
-[ZZONE] The Wolf count is off.

1438
01:08:17,760 --> 01:08:19,345
But the Hunter count is right.

1439
01:08:19,429 --> 01:08:21,681
Don't you think there are too many Wolves?

1440
01:08:21,764 --> 01:08:23,683
There are too many, I did the math.

1441
01:08:23,766 --> 01:08:26,227
Starting from Wednesday, it was weird.

1442
01:08:26,311 --> 01:08:27,937
There were too many Wolves.

1443
01:08:28,938 --> 01:08:30,189
But there are only nine of us.

1444
01:08:30,857 --> 01:08:32,859
I knew there were only nine of us.

1445
01:08:32,942 --> 01:08:35,695
And each person becomes a Wolf once,

1446
01:08:35,778 --> 01:08:39,532
so the total number of Wolves from Monday
to Saturday should add up to nine.

1447
01:08:40,658 --> 01:08:41,909
What the heck? Two...

1448
01:08:42,660 --> 01:08:44,704
But there were too many Wolves.

1449
01:08:47,206 --> 01:08:49,167
So there was a total of 15 Wolves,

1450
01:08:49,250 --> 01:08:51,044
and the number of Hunters
was exactly nine.

1451
01:08:51,127 --> 01:08:52,670
So the Wolves...

1452
01:08:52,754 --> 01:08:54,756
So that's the advantage the Seeker gets.

1453
01:08:56,716 --> 01:08:59,344
-[♪ contemplative music playing]
-[Sanghyun] There were 15 Wolves in total.

1454
01:08:59,427 --> 01:09:03,431
There was one extra Wolf every day
from Monday to Saturday.

1455
01:09:04,098 --> 01:09:06,142
That means there are six extra Wolves.

1456
01:09:06,225 --> 01:09:08,019
Maybe it's the Seeker's perk.

1457
01:09:08,102 --> 01:09:09,520
The moment I realized that,

1458
01:09:09,604 --> 01:09:12,148
I could tell that the Seeker
was up to something.

1459
01:09:12,231 --> 01:09:15,485
I believe
it's one of the Seeker's abilities.

1460
01:09:15,568 --> 01:09:17,111
There was a Wolf every day.

1461
01:09:17,195 --> 01:09:20,323
The Seeker has been a Wolf the whole time.

1462
01:09:20,948 --> 01:09:25,536
POSSIBLE SEEKER ABILITY
BEING A WOLF EVERY DAY

1463
01:09:26,329 --> 01:09:29,165
Or the Seeker might have picked someone
to become a Wolf

1464
01:09:29,248 --> 01:09:30,917
to create confusion.

1465
01:09:31,667 --> 01:09:34,754
Maybe each of us had an extra turn
without being aware of it.

1466
01:09:34,837 --> 01:09:36,381
Then, everything would add up.

1467
01:09:36,464 --> 01:09:40,009
POSSIBLE SEEKER ABILITY
LET SOMEONE ELSE BE A WOLF

1468
01:09:40,093 --> 01:09:42,887
There are nine of us,
and there are six extra Wolves.

1469
01:09:42,970 --> 01:09:46,099
There are six,
so three players didn't get that chance.

1470
01:09:46,724 --> 01:09:49,352
Let's think about why those three
didn't get a chance.

1471
01:09:49,435 --> 01:09:50,728
Maybe the order they entered?

1472
01:09:51,437 --> 01:09:54,357
It was probably given to those
who were at a disadvantage.

1473
01:09:54,440 --> 01:09:56,734
A WOLF PERK FOR THE UNDERDOGS?

1474
01:09:56,818 --> 01:09:58,945
If we look at it that way,

1475
01:09:59,028 --> 01:10:00,571
-that makes sense.
-[Horseking] Yeah.

1476
01:10:00,655 --> 01:10:01,656
I thought the same.

1477
01:10:01,739 --> 01:10:03,950
Maybe it's those
with the lowest the funds.

1478
01:10:04,033 --> 01:10:07,161
So if this theory is correct,

1479
01:10:07,245 --> 01:10:11,165
the first six people
entering the Placement Room

1480
01:10:11,249 --> 01:10:12,917
will be assigned as Wolves.

1481
01:10:13,626 --> 01:10:14,711
To know for sure,

1482
01:10:14,794 --> 01:10:16,462
-[Horseking] last place...
-[Jaegyun] Jieun entered the room first.

1483
01:10:16,546 --> 01:10:19,173
Then, we can check if she's a Wolf.

1484
01:10:19,257 --> 01:10:20,633
-[Jaegyun] On Monday?
-[Horseking] Yes.

1485
01:10:21,134 --> 01:10:24,262
[Jieun] If the Seeker gave the underdogs
the advantage of being Wolves,

1486
01:10:24,345 --> 01:10:28,933
maybe we get a Wolf marker by order
in which we enter the Placement Room.

1487
01:10:29,016 --> 01:10:30,685
That's the theory that came up.

1488
01:10:30,768 --> 01:10:31,811
To know for sure,

1489
01:10:31,894 --> 01:10:35,273
Jieun should place her Wolf marker
on any day beside Monday,

1490
01:10:35,356 --> 01:10:37,817
tag someone right away,

1491
01:10:37,900 --> 01:10:39,026
and check her score.

1492
01:10:39,110 --> 01:10:41,446
[Jieun] To see if I got points as a Wolf

1493
01:10:41,529 --> 01:10:43,114
or got points as a Dog,

1494
01:10:43,197 --> 01:10:45,575
I had to tag someone to check.

1495
01:10:45,658 --> 01:10:46,993
If I'm a Wolf,

1496
01:10:47,076 --> 01:10:48,745
I'd get three points as a bonus.

1497
01:10:48,828 --> 01:10:49,829
SHIN JIEUN

1498
01:10:49,912 --> 01:10:51,038
If I'm a Dog,

1499
01:10:51,122 --> 01:10:52,957
I'd still get one point.

1500
01:10:53,040 --> 01:10:56,169
At the start of Round 2 on Monday,
I'll be the first one to go in,

1501
01:10:56,252 --> 01:11:00,173
and we'll confirm if I'm a Wolf or not.

1502
01:11:00,256 --> 01:11:01,549
The rest has to be Dogs on Monday.

1503
01:11:01,632 --> 01:11:02,633
-[Horseking] Right.
-[Jieun] Yes.

1504
01:11:02,717 --> 01:11:04,761
[Jaegyun] Let's promise
not to pick anything else

1505
01:11:04,844 --> 01:11:06,888
-and discuss it on Monday.
-Okay.

1506
01:11:06,971 --> 01:11:08,639
A TRUCE SO EVERYONE
CAN BE DOGS ON MONDAY

1507
01:11:08,723 --> 01:11:10,516
If everyone is a Dog on Monday,

1508
01:11:10,600 --> 01:11:12,185
there should be only one Wolf.

1509
01:11:12,268 --> 01:11:13,895
Yeah, that's right.

1510
01:11:13,978 --> 01:11:15,563
On Monday,

1511
01:11:15,646 --> 01:11:17,315
if someone breaks this promise...

1512
01:11:17,398 --> 01:11:19,108
-[Jaegyun] It'll be a disaster.
-...it'll be a disaster.

1513
01:11:22,236 --> 01:11:24,989
If someone chooses
to be a Hunter or a Wolf,

1514
01:11:25,072 --> 01:11:26,783
-everything's ruined.
-[Jaegyun] Exactly.

1515
01:11:26,866 --> 01:11:29,202
If that happens,
we'll have to run around like Round 1.

1516
01:11:29,285 --> 01:11:30,995
MONDAY

1517
01:11:31,078 --> 01:11:32,830
[Junseo] Has everyone agreed to this plan?

1518
01:11:36,292 --> 01:11:37,668
[Horseking] In my opinion,

1519
01:11:38,628 --> 01:11:40,004
if the Seeker wanted to troll us,

1520
01:11:40,087 --> 01:11:41,839
they would do something else here.

1521
01:11:46,052 --> 01:11:49,180
[host] Marker placement
for Round 2 is complete.

1522
01:11:50,431 --> 01:11:52,266
[alarm blaring]

1523
01:11:52,767 --> 01:11:54,435
[host] Monday has begun.

1524
01:12:01,943 --> 01:12:04,487
We were right. And no one turned on us.

1525
01:12:05,363 --> 01:12:07,532
[gasps] There's no other Wolf now.

1526
01:12:08,115 --> 01:12:09,742
There's one Wolf.

1527
01:12:09,826 --> 01:12:11,202
[Joonsu] One Wolf. Right.

1528
01:12:12,912 --> 01:12:14,205
[Jaegyun] Our theory seems correct.

1529
01:12:14,288 --> 01:12:15,289
JIEUN IS THE WOLF?

1530
01:12:15,373 --> 01:12:16,415
I think we were right.

1531
01:12:16,499 --> 01:12:17,542
[Horseking] Based on our theory,

1532
01:12:17,625 --> 01:12:19,293
-she's in last place.
-[Jaegyun] We'll go check.

1533
01:12:19,377 --> 01:12:20,545
I might not be a Wolf.

1534
01:12:20,628 --> 01:12:22,588
-[Jaegyun] Then, we're wrong.
-Hey, go to the Dealer.

1535
01:12:22,672 --> 01:12:23,673
JIEUN TAGS JAEGYUN

1536
01:12:24,632 --> 01:12:26,926
They're checking right away.
Jieun tagged him.

1537
01:12:28,886 --> 01:12:30,763
STRAIGHT TO THE PLACEMENT ROOM
TO CHECK HER SCORE

1538
01:12:32,014 --> 01:12:33,808
I'd like to check my score.

1539
01:12:33,891 --> 01:12:35,643
[dealer] Ms. Shin Jieun's
current score is...

1540
01:12:35,726 --> 01:12:36,978
JIEUN'S ROUND 1 SCORE WAS -19

1541
01:12:37,061 --> 01:12:38,271
Jieun is a Wolf?

1542
01:12:38,354 --> 01:12:39,522
Yeah, basically.

1543
01:12:40,398 --> 01:12:43,109
If she got one point,
it proves Jieun isn't a Wolf.

1544
01:12:43,192 --> 01:12:48,155
NEGATIVE 18 POINTS MEAN DOG,
NEGATIVE 16 POINTS MEAN WOLF

1545
01:12:48,239 --> 01:12:50,616
Negative 18 points.

1546
01:12:50,700 --> 01:12:51,826
Okay, thank you.

1547
01:12:51,909 --> 01:12:54,161
CURRENT SCORE IS -18

1548
01:12:56,831 --> 01:12:57,957
Our theory was wrong.

1549
01:12:58,040 --> 01:13:00,293
-Really?
-[Jieun] I'm not a Wolf.

1550
01:13:00,376 --> 01:13:02,920
-[Jaegyun] She's not a Wolf?
-[Jieun] We got it wrong.

1551
01:13:03,004 --> 01:13:04,380
You got just one point?

1552
01:13:04,505 --> 01:13:07,008
Yes, I earned one point,
so it's at minus 18.

1553
01:13:07,091 --> 01:13:08,092
Then, that's a no.

1554
01:13:08,175 --> 01:13:09,510
TAGGING AS A WOLF EARNS 3 POINTS

1555
01:13:09,594 --> 01:13:10,887
-Then, she's not a Wolf.
-[Joonsu] She's not.

1556
01:13:10,970 --> 01:13:12,388
So, the Seeker had been a Wolf.

1557
01:13:12,471 --> 01:13:14,015
-The Seeker was a Wolf.
-[Joonsu] Wow...

1558
01:13:14,557 --> 01:13:17,810
THE SEEKER HAS BEEN A WOLF THE WHOLE TIME?

1559
01:13:17,894 --> 01:13:19,937
[Horseking] This pretty much settles it.

1560
01:13:20,021 --> 01:13:23,149
[Junseo] This must be
one of the Seeker's perks.

1561
01:13:23,232 --> 01:13:26,736
The Seeker has way more control
over the game than I thought.

1562
01:13:27,320 --> 01:13:30,197
If the Seeker was a Wolf the whole time,
let's stay here together.

1563
01:13:30,281 --> 01:13:32,199
The Wolf will try to earn more points.

1564
01:13:32,283 --> 01:13:34,535
-But we don't know who the Wolf is.
-[Jieun] The Seeker is...

1565
01:13:34,619 --> 01:13:36,954
[Horseking] I suspected Sanghyun
from the beginning,

1566
01:13:37,038 --> 01:13:40,666
and that suspicion
is moving closer to being certain.

1567
01:13:42,418 --> 01:13:43,794
[Sanghyun] Everyone suspects me.

1568
01:13:45,212 --> 01:13:48,090
All of them
suspect me of being the Seeker.

1569
01:13:48,174 --> 01:13:49,842
-This is scary.
-We should split up.

1570
01:13:49,926 --> 01:13:51,177
-Split up.
-[Sanghyun] You're splitting up?

1571
01:13:51,260 --> 01:13:52,553
-[Horseking] Huh?
-We're splitting up?

1572
01:13:52,637 --> 01:13:54,555
We have to assume our theory was wrong.

1573
01:13:54,639 --> 01:13:56,641
We can't use it any longer.
How will you find him?

1574
01:13:56,724 --> 01:13:58,851
[Sanghyun] Things don't add up,
so we go our separate ways?

1575
01:13:58,935 --> 01:13:59,936
Fine, whatever.

1576
01:14:00,019 --> 01:14:01,938
[Joonsu] We have to run away
since this is Round 2.

1577
01:14:04,273 --> 01:14:05,358
There's only one minute left.

1578
01:14:12,490 --> 01:14:13,616
I need to run away.

1579
01:14:16,494 --> 01:14:21,040
THE PLAYERS FALL INTO PANIC
AFTER THEIR THEORY FALLS APART

1580
01:14:21,123 --> 01:14:24,752
[Junseo] I thought this was part
of the Seeker's strategy to confuse us.

1581
01:14:25,836 --> 01:14:28,631
[Jimin] I felt like
I I couldn't take action anymore.

1582
01:14:29,757 --> 01:14:32,385
[Eunsil] I needed to be
a little more careful.

1583
01:14:35,012 --> 01:14:38,015
EVERYONE HAS LEFT

1584
01:14:45,314 --> 01:14:46,774
SOMETHING MOVES

1585
01:14:50,903 --> 01:14:53,489
After the first round,
I kept thinking about it.

1586
01:14:53,572 --> 01:14:56,450
Why is there one extra Wolf?

1587
01:14:56,534 --> 01:14:59,787
So when everyone dispersed in Round 2,

1588
01:14:59,870 --> 01:15:02,206
I hid right next to the Placement Room.

1589
01:15:04,875 --> 01:15:08,129
[alarm blaring]

1590
01:15:08,754 --> 01:15:10,673
[host] Tuesday has begun.

1591
01:15:13,843 --> 01:15:17,388
Looking back,
when I thought about the Dealer Room

1592
01:15:17,471 --> 01:15:21,017
or Placement Room
right from the start at Round 1,

1593
01:15:21,100 --> 01:15:22,476
something felt off.

1594
01:15:23,352 --> 01:15:26,564
I don't know why,
but something kept bothering me.

1595
01:15:28,024 --> 01:15:30,651
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

1596
01:15:30,735 --> 01:15:32,653
Something's definitely going on here.

1597
01:15:33,195 --> 01:15:35,072
[Jimin] Don't you think
there are too many Wolves?

1598
01:15:35,156 --> 01:15:36,407
[Jaegyun] But there are only nine of us.

1599
01:15:36,490 --> 01:15:37,992
[ZZONE] The Wolf count is off.

1600
01:15:38,075 --> 01:15:39,285
Something's off.

1601
01:15:42,371 --> 01:15:45,416
[host] The second Main Match is
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves."

1602
01:15:45,499 --> 01:15:47,334
Do wolves usually have
different-colored eyes?

1603
01:15:47,418 --> 01:15:49,628
[Jaegyun] It's heterochromia.
Different colored eyes.

1604
01:15:51,172 --> 01:15:52,173
[Sanghyun] The Seeker.

1605
01:15:53,090 --> 01:15:54,091
Heterochromia.

1606
01:15:54,884 --> 01:15:55,885
A Wolf Seeker.

1607
01:16:00,723 --> 01:16:01,724
I got it.

1608
01:16:03,225 --> 01:16:05,227
[♪ ominous music playing]

1609
01:16:24,163 --> 01:16:26,165
Translated by Youji Kim
